{"pair_id": "pair_ast_2949894e5b36", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "positive", "filler": "long primary PD excerpt for astrology_west (Ptolemy Tetrabiblos fresh)", "span": "Ptolemy's Tetrabiblos, Book I: Of the Zodiacal Circle and its Divisions. The circle of the Zodiac is divided into twelve equal parts, called signs, each of which contains thirty degrees. The first sign is Aries, which begins at the vernal equinox. The signs are: Aries, Taurus, Gemini, Cancer, Leo, Virgo, Libra, Scorpio, Sagittarius, Capricorn, Aquarius, Pisces.", "atom_id": "pd.astrology_west.386578f6", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
