{"pair_id": "pair_low_cab19cf0ebeb", "family_id": "mesopotamia", "role": "positive", "filler": "long primary PD excerpt for mesopotamia (continued low family boost)", "span": "Nevertheless these rulers, although appearing in the pretentious nomenclature as gods, appear to have been real historic personages. ( The name Gilgamish was originally written _dGi-bil-aga-mi\u0161_, and means \u201cThe fire god ( _Gibil_) is a commander,\u201d abbreviated to _dGi-bil-ga-mi\u0161_, and _dGi(\u0161)-bil-ga-mi\u0161_, a form which by full labialization of _b_ to _u\u032f_ was finally contracted to _dGi-il-ga-mi\u0161_. ( Throughout the new text the name is written with the abbreviation _dGi(\u0161)_, ( whereas the standard ", "atom_id": "pd.mesopotamia.279b812b", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "pair_low_64727d052488", "family_id": "mesopotamia", "role": "positive", "filler": "long primary PD excerpt for mesopotamia (continued low family boost)", "span": "The Enuma Elish tablet describes how Marduk defeats the chaos dragon Tiamat and creates the world from her body. The text was recited during the New Year festival to renew the cosmic order and legitimize the king. It establishes the hierarchy of the gods and the role of Babylon as the center of the world.", "atom_id": "pd.mesopotamia.d64040d3", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
