{"pair_id": "pair_low_b4f3919c1459", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "positive", "filler": "long primary PD excerpt for shinto_onmyodo (continued low family boost)", "span": "So the Great August Deity the Male-Who-Invites said to His Swift-Impetuous-Male-Augustness: \u201cHow is it that, instead of ruling the land with which I charged thee, thou dost wail and weep?\u201d He replied, saying: \u201cI[\\[7\\]](https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/#cite_note-7) wail because I wish \u200bto depart to my deceased mother\u2019s[\\[8\\]](https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/#cite_note-8) land, to the Nether Distant Land.\u201d[\\[9\\]](https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/#cite_note-9) Then the Great August Deity the Male-Who-I", "atom_id": "pd.shinto_onmyodo.cf381d23", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "pair_low_8342c892ca50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "positive", "filler": "long primary PD excerpt for shinto_onmyodo (continued low family boost)", "span": "XII.\u2014The Crying and Weeping of His Impetuous-Male-Augustness.\\] So while \\[the other two Deities\\] each \\[assumed his and her\\] rule according to the command with which \\[their father\\] had deigned to charge them, His-Swift-Impetuous-Male-Augustness did not \\[assume the\\] rule \\[of\\] the dominion with which he had been charged, but cried and wept till his eight-grasp beard[\\[1\\]](https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/#cite_note-1) reached to the pit of his stomach.[\\[2\\]](https://en.wikisource.org/wiki", "atom_id": "pd.shinto_onmyodo.3eb37590", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
