{"pair_id": "pair_low_d825493e600a", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "positive", "filler": "long primary PD excerpt for mesoamerica (continued low family boost)", "span": "Payne writes: ( \u201cThe fact that the worship of Quetzalcohuatl under the name of Cuculcan or Gucumatz was extensively prevalent in Yucatan and Central America, while no trace is found of the worship of Tezcatlipoca, strongly suggests that the founders of the Central American pueblos (the Toltecs) were, in fact, devotees of Quetzalcohuatl, who preferred exile and adventure in strange lands to accepting a religious innovation which was intolerable to them.\u201d That Quetzalcohuatl was not an aboriginal ", "atom_id": "pd.mesoamerica.59f41d56", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
