{"pair_id": "pair_24boost_8661208e5304", "family_id": "islamic_occult_pd", "role": "positive", "filler": "primary PD excerpt for islamic_occult_pd (continue boost for min 24 families)", "span": "We acknowledge the individuals\u2014giants of scholarship, one and all\u2014whose pioneering efforts form the bedrock of this work: David Pingree, Martin Pless- ner, and Helmut Ritter We are likewise grateful to the more recent translation efforts of Davide Arecco, Ida Li Vigni, Paolo A Rossi, Stefano Zufh, B\u00e9atrice Bakhouche, Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Fauquier, Brigitte P\u00e9rez-Jean, John Michael Greer, and Christopher Warnock, whose work we inevitably had to take into account. xii ACKNOWLEDGMENTS We would like to thank S.", "atom_id": "pd.islamic_occult_pd.9bf83ee0", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "pair_24boost_687254b75b49", "family_id": "islamic_occult_pd", "role": "positive", "filler": "primary PD excerpt for islamic_occult_pd (continue boost for min 24 families)", "span": "The unity of God is pre- served since the planetary powers are understood as astral volitional forces that constitute the hidden inner workings of a cosmos ruled entirely by God\u2019s will.\u201d For al-Qurtubi, magic is the inevitable consequence of a zealous philo- sophical life\u00bb? Regarding the question of efficacy, the practical elements of the Picatrix concerning ritual magic are founded upon a consistent syncretic philosophical worldview The praises of wisdom and true science in the open- ing portio", "atom_id": "pd.islamic_occult_pd.da72e002", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "pair_24boost_905fcfaac31a", "family_id": "islamic_occult_pd", "role": "positive", "filler": "primary PD excerpt for islamic_occult_pd (continue boost for min 24 families)", "span": "Although we certainly recognize these etymological transformations, the magic in the Picatrix is strictly concerned with invoking the powers of spirits belonging to specific heavenly bodies, and there are no forms of divination INTRODUCTION 11 pertaining to the dead in its pages (though the dismembered body parts of humans and sacrificial animals do occasionally appear as ritual compo- nents).\u00b0\u00b0 While this word nigromancia pertains to the invocation of occult forces, the spirits invoked are not ", "atom_id": "pd.islamic_occult_pd.8566d781", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "pair_24boost_858145820bc8", "family_id": "islamic_occult_pd", "role": "positive", "filler": "primary PD excerpt for islamic_occult_pd (continue boost for min 24 families)", "span": "Its simplicity appealed both to the scientific perspective of the time and to theologians In the Book of 24 Philosophers, Hermes Tris- megistus defines God as \u201can infinite sphere whose center is everywhere and whose circumference is nowhere.\u201d\u00ae Implicit to the Picatrix is a vision of the world that Aristotle had organized and that later figues such as Ptolomy, al- Kindi, and Abu Ma\u2018Shar would expound upon in much detail It is a vision of the universe as a series of concentric spheres made of some", "atom_id": "pd.islamic_occult_pd.c3e4649b", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "pair_24boost_2c337c942121", "family_id": "islamic_occult_pd", "role": "positive", "filler": "primary PD excerpt for islamic_occult_pd (continue boost for min 24 families)", "span": "Those who secretly practiced nigromancia considered it the natural outcome, the consummation, of all medieval science, wisdom, and philosophy Thus, in our opinion, it is not entirely correct to connect the Pica- trix with necromancy, black magic, or any form of objectionable sorcery For this reason, we have ultimately opted to render nigromancia with the nebulous word \u201cmagic\u201d in our translation, and we hope this interpretation will serve to 12 PICATRIX clean up the sullied reputation that easily", "atom_id": "pd.islamic_occult_pd.db4a8a9a", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "pair_24boost_f88ab731999c", "family_id": "islamic_occult_pd", "role": "positive", "filler": "primary PD excerpt for islamic_occult_pd (continue boost for min 24 families)", "span": "Picatrix on planetary images and the making of astrological talismans for specific purposes.", "atom_id": "pd.islamic_occult_pd.8c99ba1a", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "pair_24boost_35f720d6af0e", "family_id": "islamic_occult_pd", "role": "positive", "filler": "primary PD excerpt for islamic_occult_pd (continue boost for min 24 families)", "span": "The cryptic and labyrinthine nature of the Picatrix is one of the more evident aspects of its composer\u2019s heightened sense of esoteric elitism. 10 PICATRIX \u201cIfthis knowledge were revealed to humankind,\u201d he writes, \u201cit would destroy the universe\u201d (Prologue .3) We are told that its obscure style and figurative speech is in the interest of \u201chonesty and goodwill\u201d and that this is done to protect humankind against its own ambition\u2014against men who would operate for themselves rather than \u201cfor the good,", "atom_id": "pd.islamic_occult_pd.d50c617b", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "pair_24boost_d0e5eed7f6ed", "family_id": "islamic_occult_pd", "role": "positive", "filler": "primary PD excerpt for islamic_occult_pd (continue boost for min 24 families)", "span": "PICATRIX A MEDIEVAL TREATISE ON ASTRAL MAGIC TRANSLATED WITH AN INTRODUCTION BY DAN ATTRELL AND DAVID PORRECA Based on the Latin edition by David Pingree THE PENNSYLVANIA STATE UNIVERSITY PRESS UNIVERSITY PARK, PENNSYLVANIA Library of Congress Cataloging-in- Publication Data Names: Majriti, Maslamah ibn Ahmad, -1004?, author. | Attrell, Dan, 1988- editor, translator. | Porreca, David, 1974- editor, translator Title: Picatrix : a medieval treatise on astral magic / edited and translated by Dan At", "atom_id": "pd.islamic_occult_pd.9be78bf2", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "pair_24boost_a6c1c6571ef8", "family_id": "grimoire", "role": "positive", "filler": "primary PD excerpt for grimoire (continue boost for min 24 families)", "span": "The book includes charms against witchcraft and for finding hidden treasure using traditional cunning man techniques.", "atom_id": "pd.grimoire.e1a570c3", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "pair_24boost_7fff495fb54a", "family_id": "grimoire", "role": "positive", "filler": "primary PD excerpt for grimoire (continue boost for min 24 families)", "span": "The Grimoire of Arthur Gauntlet A 17th century London Cunning-man book of charms, conjurations and prayers Includes material from the Heptameron, the Arbatel, the Discoverie of Witchcraft.", "atom_id": "pd.grimoire.b31aa753", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "pair_24boost_9c27a4289d50", "family_id": "grimoire", "role": "positive", "filler": "primary PD excerpt for grimoire (continue boost for min 24 families)", "span": "Thus _Och_, the prince of Solar things, presides over the preparation or development of gold naturally in the veins of the earth--that is to say, he is the Mineralogist in Chief of Nature; he presides also over the quicker preparation of the same metal by means of chemical art--that is, he is the Prince of Alchemists; and, finally, he makes gold in a moment by Magic. It is in this way p. 30 that Ceremonial Magic connects with while it assumes to transcend Hermetic Art. ( There is another curious", "atom_id": "pd.grimoire.e20ba618", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "pair_24boost_134bf19d79b1", "family_id": "grimoire", "role": "positive", "filler": "primary PD excerpt for grimoire (continue boost for min 24 families)", "span": "A charm to cause an enemy to lose their way involves writing the person's name backward on a piece of paper and burying it with a dead toad. The text warns that such operations should only be undertaken with pure intent, lest the magic rebound on the operator.", "atom_id": "pd.grimoire.dced88b0", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "pair_24boost_5a30b80f8852", "family_id": "grimoire", "role": "positive", "filler": "primary PD excerpt for grimoire (continue boost for min 24 families)", "span": "The mottoes on the title are _Summum Sapienti\u00e6 Studium_ and _In omnibus consule Dominum, et nihil cogites, dicas, facias, quod tibi Deus non consuluerit_. 04. ( The possibility is warranted by references in the 30th and 31st Aphorisms to some obscure points of Italian history. It is said that by a judgment of the Magicians it was decreed that no Italian should reign over the kingdom of Naples; now the monarch at the time was an Italian, and he was dethroned in due course. To restore the national", "atom_id": "pd.grimoire.e70a736d", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "pair_24boost_0fee5df68549", "family_id": "grimoire", "role": "positive", "filler": "primary PD excerpt for grimoire (continue boost for min 24 families)", "span": "It should be observed that the _Arbatel_ has no connection with the cycle, hereinafter considered, of the Keys of Solomon, p. 28 and it is permeated with Christian ideas. The authorship is completely unknown. Arbatel, or \u05d0\u05e8\u05d1\u05e2\u05ea\u05d0\u05dc {Hebrew _ARBOTAL_}, is probably not an assumed name, but indicative of an instructing or revealing Angel. The use of this Hebrew term is, however, peculiar in connection with the fact that the references to the Old Testament are few and unimportant, while the sayings of ", "atom_id": "pd.grimoire.0c1dc6c7", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "pair_24boost_be96b30faf33", "family_id": "grimoire", "role": "positive", "filler": "primary PD excerpt for grimoire (continue boost for min 24 families)", "span": "( Hide Close navigation ( - ( Categories - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( Pages - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( Toggle Sideba", "atom_id": "pd.grimoire.2d02ebce", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "pair_24boost_b78aa99931ae", "family_id": "grimoire", "role": "positive", "filler": "primary PD excerpt for grimoire (continue boost for min 24 families)", "span": "It is, therefore, better for the student, says the _Arbatel_, to work only by the offices of the Spirits, without their names; should he be pre-ordained to attain the Art of Magic, the other parts of that Art will offer themselves of their own accord. The sources of occult wisdom, it proceeds, are, firstly, in God; secondly, in spiritual essences--that is to say, the Angelical Hierarchy; thirdly, in corporeal creatures, the reference being probably to the _signatura rerum_ of Paracelsus; fourthl", "atom_id": "pd.grimoire.dd195f99", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
