{"pair_id": "pair_26boost_c20f5374bba9", "family_id": "andes_amazon", "role": "positive", "filler": "long primary PD excerpt for andes_amazon (continue low family boost)", "span": "Scherzer at once made a copy of the Spanish translation of the manuscript, which he published at Vienna in 1856 under the title of \u201cLas Historias del origen de los Indios de Guatemala, par el R P F Francisco Ximenes.\u201d The Abb\u00e9 Brasseur also took a copy of the original, which he published at Paris in 1861, with the title \u201cVuh Popol: Le Livre Sacr\u00e9 de Quich\u00e9s, et les Mythes de l\u2019Antiquit\u00e9 Am\u00e9ricaine.\u201d In this work the Kich\u00e9 original and the Abbe\u2019s French translation are set forth side by side Unfo", "atom_id": "pd.andes_amazon.017b9f5c", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "pair_26boost_c9eb867d02f0", "family_id": "andes_amazon", "role": "positive", "filler": "long primary PD excerpt for andes_amazon (continue low family boost)", "span": "However this may apply to the reputed compositions of the Goidelic bard, there can be no doubt that it can be used with justice as regards the \u201cPopol Vuh.\u201d To any one who has given it a careful examination it must be abundantly evident that it is a composition that has passed through several stages of development; that it is unquestionably of aboriginal origin; and that it has only been influenced by European thought in a secondary and unessential manner The very fact that it was composed in the", "atom_id": "pd.andes_amazon.4f027466", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "pair_26boost_2201f87866c7", "family_id": "andes_amazon", "role": "positive", "filler": "long primary PD excerpt for andes_amazon (continue low family boost)", "span": "The Abb\u00e9 Brasseur de Bourbourg, a profound student of American arch\u00e6ology and languages (whose euhemeristic interpretations of the Mexican \\( are as worthless as the priceless materials he unearthed are valuable) deplored, in a letter to the Duc de Valmy, ( the supposed loss of the \u201cPopol Vuh,\u201d which he was aware had been made use of early in the nineteenth century by a certain Don Felix Cabrera Dr C Scherzer, an Austrian scholar, thus made aware of its value, paid a visit to the Republic of Gua", "atom_id": "pd.andes_amazon.574f0c95", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "pair_26boost_989b04f927da", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "positive", "filler": "long primary PD excerpt for astrology_west (continue low family boost)", "span": "Ptolemy's Tetrabiblos, Book I: Of the Zodiacal Circle and its Divisions. The circle of the Zodiac is divided into twelve equal parts, called signs, each of which contains thirty degrees. The first sign is Aries, which begins at the vernal equinox. The signs are: Aries, Taurus, Gemini, Cancer, Leo, Virgo, Libra, Scorpio, Sagittarius, Capricorn, Aquarius, Pisces.", "atom_id": "pd.astrology_west.386578f6", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "pair_26boost_1c4fa93daca1", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "positive", "filler": "long primary PD excerpt for astrology_west (continue low family boost)", "span": "Helps us pay the bills. ## Discussion Community conversation ### Discussions are coming soon Join conversations around this text and its interpretations Advertisement ( Why ads? Advertisement ( Why ads? ( \\\\ The archive, offlineOwn the Wisdom of the AgesEvery text in the library on a single USB drive Read offline, cite freely, keep forever No subscription required.\\\\ \\\\ Get the drive$127.00]( Advertisement ( Why ads? PT Title # Ptolemy's Tetrabiblos Author Claudius Ptolemy Translated by J M Ashm", "atom_id": "pd.astrology_west.ea8b57fb", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "pair_26boost_d0bf028dc9e3", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "positive", "filler": "long primary PD excerpt for astrology_west (continue low family boost)", "span": "It professes to be a translation from the original text of Ptolemy ; and\\ so likewise does the translation printed at Basle, as above quoted.\\ \\ 2 This assertion is applicable only to Proclus\u2019s Paraphrase. \u2018There were\\ several prior translations of the original Tetrabiblos in Latin and Arabic; and\\ it appears by an extract from the Bibliotheca Greca of Fabricius [which will be\\ found in a subsequent page], that a Latin version, done from the Arabic, was\\ printed at Venice as early as the year 14", "atom_id": "pd.astrology_west.44fbb9c0", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "pair_26boost_9c7e2adf46cf", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "positive", "filler": "long primary PD excerpt for astrology_west (continue low family boost)", "span": "Even this second publica-\\ tion, worthless as it intrinsically is, can rarely now be met with, and, like\\ the former, only at a very heavy price.\\ \\ The present Translation has been made from Proclus\u2019s Greek Para-\\ phrase of Prolemy\u2019s original text ; the edition followed is that of the\\ Elzevirs, dated in 1635.4 But, in the course of translation, continual\\ references have been also had to various editions of the original text, in\\ order to ascertain the proper acceptation of doubtful passages T", "atom_id": "pd.astrology_west.ab9e9d80", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
