{"pair_id": "pair_26boost_e7f476705fa7", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "positive", "filler": "long primary PD excerpt for coptic_gnostic (continue low family boost)", "span": "The Pistis Sopha is a startling blend of primitive Christianity and Hellenic Paganism, with other elements such as reincarnation, Astrology, Mystery religion and Hermetic magic The Goddess makes an appearance in the guise of Sophia, a fallen angel The text is notable because the female disciples of Jesus are treated as active participants in the discourse, in a way that would be unimaginable in later Christianity Tensions between the men and women disciples are not glossed over On p. 47, Peter c", "atom_id": "pd.coptic_gnostic.b715f711", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
