{"pair_id": "pair_26boost_ee5f79969ce8", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "positive", "filler": "long primary PD excerpt for coptic_gnostic (continue low family boost)", "span": "In fact, the only other im- portant relic of the Gnosis w^hich is so far known to have withstood the ravages of time and escaped the destruction of Christian and Mohammedan vandalism, is the Coptic papyrus, known as the Codex Brucianus and preserved in the Bodleian at Oxford, to which reference will be made later on In the same library there is also another Coptic MS., a small quarto of 236 pages, entitled Treatise on the Mysteries of the Greek Letters, to which an Arabic translation is appended", "atom_id": "pd.coptic_gnostic.32b5f3f8", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
