{"pair_id": "pair_29boost_1e5a39fbf863", "family_id": "mystery_cults", "role": "positive", "filler": "long primary PD excerpt for mystery_cults (continue low family boost)", "span": "TO LIKNITUS BACCHUS \\ _The Fumigation from Manna._ Liknitan Bacchus \\, bearer of the vine, thee I invoke to bless these rites divine: Florid and gay, of nymphs the blossom bright, and of fair Venus \\, Goddess of delight, 'Tis thine mad footsteps with mad nymphs to beat, dancing thro' groves with lightly leaping feet: From Jove's \\ high counsels nurst by Proserpine \\, and born the dread of all the pow'rs divine: Come, blessed pow'r, regard thy suppliant's voice, propitious come, and in these rite", "atom_id": "pd.mystery_cults.fd81fde6", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "pair_29boost_09d577e700f0", "family_id": "mystery_cults", "role": "positive", "filler": "long primary PD excerpt for mystery_cults (continue low family boost)", "span": "TO MISES \\ _The Fumigation from Storax._ Call Thesmophorus, spermatic God \\, of various names, who bears the leafy rod: Mises \\, ineffable, pure, sacred queen, two-fold Iacchus, male and female seen: Illustr'ous, whether to rejoice is thine in incense offer'd, in the fane divine; Or if in Phrygia most thy soul delights, performing with thy mother sacred rites; Or if the land of Cyprus is thy care, well pleas'd to dwell with Cytherea \\ fair; Or if exulting in the fertile plains with thy dark moth", "atom_id": "pd.mystery_cults.db76a2e2", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "pair_29boost_d3d624675851", "family_id": "mystery_cults", "role": "positive", "filler": "long primary PD excerpt for mystery_cults (continue low family boost)", "span": "TO THE GRACES \\ _The Fumigation from Storax._ Hear me, illustrious Graces \\, mighty nam'd, from Jove descended and Eunomia fam'd; Thalia, and Aglaia fair and bright, and blest Euphrosyne whom joys delight: Mothers of mirth, all lovely to the view, pleasure abundant pure belongs to you: Various, forever flourishing and fair, desir'd by mortals, much invok'd in pray'r: Circling, dark-ey'd, delightful to mankind, come, and your mystics bless with bounteous mind. ### \\ LX TO NEMESIS _A Hymn._ Thee, ", "atom_id": "pd.mystery_cults.863399f6", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "pair_29boost_e239df8eb184", "family_id": "mystery_cults", "role": "positive", "filler": "long primary PD excerpt for mystery_cults (continue low family boost)", "span": "TO THE NYMPHS \\ _The Fumigation from Aromatics._ Nymphs, who from Ocean's \\ stream derive your birth, who dwell in liquid caverns of the earth Nurses of Bacchus \\ secret-coursing pow'r, who fruits sustain, and nourish ev'ry flow'r: Earthly, rejoicing, who in meadows dwell, and caves and dens, whose depths extend to hell: Holy, oblique, who swiftly soar thro' air, fountains and dews, and mazy streams your care: Seen and unseen, who joy with wand'rings wide and gentle course, thro' flow'ry vales t", "atom_id": "pd.mystery_cults.8e646ae2", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "pair_29boost_466896e3ee45", "family_id": "mystery_cults", "role": "positive", "filler": "long primary PD excerpt for mystery_cults (continue low family boost)", "span": "Toggle navigation [Theoi Project - Classical Texts\\\\ Library]( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( - ( [Classical Texts\\\\ Library]( >\\> [Orphic\\\\ Hymns]( >\\> Hymns 41-86 # ORPHIC HYMNS 41 - 86 ### ORPHIC HYMNS CONTENTS ( ( To Musaeus ( To Prothyraea ( To Nyx (Night) ( To Uranus (the Sky) ( To Aether ( To Protogonus ( To Astron (the Stars) ( To Helius (the Sun) ( To Selene (the Moon) ( To Phusis (Nature) ( To Pan ( To Heracles ( To Cronus ( To R", "atom_id": "pd.mystery_cults.6bb9bcb7", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
