{"pair_id": "corr.runes_eddic.symbol.b7f285", "family_id": "runes_eddic", "role": "symbol", "filler": "There are competent translations in both Norwegian and Swedish. The", "span": "lack of any complete and adequately annotated English rendering in", "atom_id": "0af0bc620bc4", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.runes_eddic.concept.2bfced", "family_id": "runes_eddic", "role": "concept", "filler": "The hero poems give us, in its oldest and most", "span": "vivid extant form, the story of Sigurth, Brynhild, and Atli,", "atom_id": "c7cb46f000f4", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.runes_eddic.text.a82fec", "family_id": "runes_eddic", "role": "text", "filler": "Preserved in various manuscripts of the thirteenth and early fourteenth", "span": "centuries is a prose work consisting of a very extensive", "atom_id": "daa2c8d2fbe3", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.runes_eddic.letter.f86d2a", "family_id": "runes_eddic", "role": "letter", "filler": "So matters stood when, in 1643, Brynjolfur Sveinsson, Bishop of", "span": "Skalholt, discovered a manuscript, clearly written as early as 1300,", "atom_id": "e2ddfc09dbe4", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.runes_eddic.practice.537dda", "family_id": "runes_eddic", "role": "practice", "filler": "Brodeur's rendering of Snorri's work. From all this it is", "span": "evident that the Poetic Edda , as we now know", "atom_id": "c6a45f660327", "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
