{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.concept.0e13f6", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "concept", "filler": "The name \u201cPopol Vuh\u201d signifies \u201cRecord of the Community,\u201d and", "span": "its literal translation is \u201cBook of the Mat,\u201d from the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.text.dca613", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "text", "filler": "Of this tongue the \u201cPopol Vuh\u201d is practically the only", "span": "monument; at all events the only work by a native", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.letter.5851ce", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "letter", "filler": "Such, then, were the people whose mythology produced the body", "span": "of tradition and mythi-history known as the \u201cPopol Vuh\u201d; and", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.practice.4e1a67", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "practice", "filler": "And it is said that their posterity are the little", "span": "monkeys who live in the woods. [ Contents ] The", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.planet.d1ca0d", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "planet", "filler": "The hero-gods, who lay concealed within the foliage, now added", "span": "injury to theft by hurling at Vukub-Cakix a dart from", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.element.ef76c4", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "element", "filler": "Next they removed his eyes of emerald, upon which his", "span": "death speedily followed, as did that of his wife Chimalmat.", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.symbol.16f4f0", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "symbol", "filler": "The hero-gods constructed an artificial crab which [ 15 ]", "span": "they placed in a cavern at the bottom of a", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.concept.0e13f6", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "concept", "filler": "All of them were addicted to the recreation of dicing", "span": "and playing at ball, and a spectator of their pastimes", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.text.dca613", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "text", "filler": "All in Xibalba were forbidden the fruit of that tree.", "span": "But one person in Xibalba had resolved to disobey the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.letter.5851ce", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "letter", "filler": "Returning at night from hunting, they smeared their faces and", "span": "hands with dirt so that Xmucane might be deceived into", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.practice.4e1a67", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "practice", "filler": "The message, however, was duly delivered, and the players returned", "span": "home to take leave of their grandmother and mother. Before", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.planet.d1ca0d", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "planet", "filler": "The brothers, however, had at their beck and call a", "span": "swarm of ants, which entered the royal gardens on the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.element.ef76c4", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "element", "filler": "Their bones were beaten to powder and thrown into the", "span": "river, where they sank, and were transformed into young men.", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.symbol.16f4f0", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "symbol", "filler": "These young men were busied at Xibalba with paying fitting", "span": "funeral honours to their father and uncle, who now mounted", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.concept.0e13f6", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "concept", "filler": "These were the ancestors of the Kich\u00e9s only. Then were", "span": "created the ancestors of other peoples. They were ignorant of", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.text.dca613", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "text", "filler": "At length they came to a mountain [ 26 ]", "span": "which they called Hacavitz, after one of their gods, and", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.letter.5851ce", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "letter", "filler": "\u201cIn performing this journey they expended many years and suffered", "span": "extraordinary hardships.\u201d Nimaquich\u00e9 was succeeded by his son Aexopil, from", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.practice.4e1a67", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "practice", "filler": "But another and more important question arises in connection with", "span": "the initial chapters of the \u201cPopol Vuh\u201d\u2014those which give an", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.planet.d1ca0d", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "planet", "filler": "That the Mayan civilisation was of very considerable antiquity is", "span": "possible, although no adequate proof exists for the assumption. This", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.element.ef76c4", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "element", "filler": "2 The Zu\u00f1is imagined that Awonawilona, the All-father, so impregnated", "span": "the waters that a scum appeared upon their surface which", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.symbol.16f4f0", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "symbol", "filler": "He found they abounded too much with those ideas that", "span": "only belong to an early state of society to be", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.concept.0e13f6", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "concept", "filler": "In Mexico Ixtlilxochitl, and in Peru Garcilasso de la Vega,", "span": "wrote exhaustive treatises upon the history and customs of their", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.text.dca613", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "text", "filler": "[ 36 ] 1 \u201cHistory of the Fur Trade,\u201d Mackenzie,", "span": "p. 83. \u2191 2 Schoolcraft, \u201cIndian Tribes,\u201d i. p. 266.", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.letter.5851ce", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "letter", "filler": "These, we will remember, appeared in the myth of Vukub-Cakix", "span": "and elsewhere. The first appears to apply to the paternal", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.practice.4e1a67", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "practice", "filler": "Cucumatz is one and the same with the Nahuatlacan\u2014or, more", "span": "properly speaking, Toltecan Quetzalcohuatl. The name is compounded from two", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.planet.d1ca0d", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "planet", "filler": "Mr. Payne writes: 2 \u201cThe fact that the worship of", "span": "Quetzalcohuatl under the name of Cuculcan or Gucumatz was extensively", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.element.ef76c4", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "element", "filler": "Hurakan is also alluded to in the \u201cPopol Vuh,\u201d as", "span": "\u201cThe Strong Serpent,\u201d and \u201cHe who hurls below,\u201d referring to", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.symbol.16f4f0", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "symbol", "filler": "That they were of the earth as truly as were", "span": "the Jotuns of Scandinavian mythology there can be no doubt.", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.concept.0e13f6", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "concept", "filler": "The \u201cPopol Vuh\u201d definitely describes Xibalba as the metropolis of", "span": "an \u201cUnderworld\u201d; and with such examples as that of the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.text.dca613", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "text", "filler": "They were but annoyers and opposers of men, and, in", "span": "truth, they were not regarded as gods .\u201d If not", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.letter.5851ce", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "letter", "filler": "The Xibalbans, or aborigines, were perhaps cave- or earth-dwellers like", "span": "the Picts of Scottish folk-lore, gnomeish, and full of elvish", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.practice.4e1a67", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "practice", "filler": "But by the period of the formation of the myth", "span": "it is probable that Xibalba had become confounded with the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.planet.d1ca0d", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "planet", "filler": "The Aztecs called this river Chicunoapa, the Nine Rivers, where", "span": "the departed must pay toll to a dog and a", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.element.ef76c4", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "element", "filler": "This may have resembled the Mexican game of tlachtli, which", "span": "was played in an enclosed court with a rubber ball", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.symbol.16f4f0", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "symbol", "filler": "He multiplies. Gods are given to each tribe. These he", "span": "bears to a new country. In fact we have a", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.concept.0e13f6", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "concept", "filler": "It is there where they were founded in Colhuacan. They", "span": "were the colonists of it since they landed there, coming", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.text.dca613", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "text", "filler": "To begin with, Landa, Cogolludo, and Las Casas confine themselves", "span": "more to Yucatan proper than to Guatemala, and their remarks", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.letter.5851ce", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "letter", "filler": "Four times the old man spread his legs. Now the", "span": "opossum spreads his legs\u201d\u2014 Say the people. 12 [ 55", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.practice.4e1a67", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "practice", "filler": "der Miss. der evang. Br\u00fcder .\u201d \u2191 9 \u201cRel. de", "span": "la Nouv. France,\u201d 1636. \u2191 10 J. W. Fewkes in", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
