{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.concept.0e13f6", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "concept", "filler": "The knowledge of this staple, he infers, spread rapidly among", "span": "the northern peoples, and induced them to hasten their southern", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.text.dca613", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "text", "filler": "Gucumatz, it will be remembered, is Quetzalcohuatl in another form,", "span": "and [ 63 ] the latter is often represented in", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.mesoamerica.letter.5851ce", "family_id": "mesoamerica", "role": "letter", "filler": "[ 64 ] [ Contents ] Printed by Ballantyne &", "span": "Co. Limited Tavistock Street, Covent Garden, London Table of Contents", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.planet.e2a224", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "planet", "filler": "Give up what is before, give up what is behind,", "span": "give up what is between, when thou goest to the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.element.af7c1d", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "element", "filler": "[pg 153] THE UPANISHADS Translation by F. Max M\u00fcller [pg", "span": "155] INTRODUCTION The \"Upanishads\" are reckoned to be from a", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.symbol.b456f2", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "symbol", "filler": "The seer, in order to communicate to the world the", "span": "result of his meditations, seems to catch at every symbol", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.concept.6471b4", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "concept", "filler": "E.W. [pg 157] THE UPANISHADS KAUSH\u00ceTAKI-UPANISHAD THE COUCH OF BRAHMAN", "span": "Kitra G\u00e2ngy\u00e2yani, wishing to perform a sacrifice, chose \u00c2runi Udd\u00e2laka,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.text.ff96be", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "text", "filler": "But if a man does not object, then the moon", "span": "sends him down as rain upon this earth. And according", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.letter.5c4afd", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "letter", "filler": "In that world there is the lake \u00c2ra, the moments", "span": "called Yeshtiha, the river Vigar\u00e2, i.e., age-less, the tree Ily\u00e2,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.practice.22a45d", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "practice", "filler": "He comes to the river Vigar\u00e2, and crosses it by", "span": "the mind alone, and there shakes off his good and", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.planet.e2a224", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "planet", "filler": "The past and the future are its eastern feet; prosperity", "span": "and earth its western feet; the S\u00e2man verses, Brihad and", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.element.af7c1d", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "element", "filler": "\"Of this pr\u00e2na, which is Brahman, the mind is the", "span": "messenger, speech the housekeeper, the eye the guard, the ear", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.symbol.b456f2", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "symbol", "filler": "For him who knows this, there is this Upanishad, or", "span": "secret vow, [pg 162] 'Beg not!' As a man who", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.concept.6471b4", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "concept", "filler": "Whatever other oblations there are (those, e.g., of the ordinary", "span": "Agni-hotri, consisting of milk and other things), they have an", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.text.ff96be", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "text", "filler": "This Brahman shines forth indeed when the fire burns, and", "span": "it dies when it burns not. Its splendor goes to", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.letter.5c4afd", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "letter", "filler": "Its splendor goes to the breath alone, and the life", "span": "to breath. \"Thus all these deities (the senses, etc.), having", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.practice.22a45d", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "practice", "filler": "And in the same manner he who knows this, having", "span": "recognized the pre\u00ebminence in pr\u00e2na, and having comprehended life alone", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.planet.e2a224", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "planet", "filler": "The father calls after him: 'May fame, glory of countenance,", "span": "and honor always follow thee.' Then the other looks back", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.element.af7c1d", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "element", "filler": "If he is going to commit a sin, the bloom", "span": "does not depart from his face. I am pr\u00e2na, meditate", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.symbol.b456f2", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "symbol", "filler": "But pr\u00e2na alone is the conscious self, and having laid", "span": "hold of this body, it makes it rise up. Therefore", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.concept.6471b4", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "concept", "filler": "The nose gives up to him all odors, so that", "span": "by scent he obtains all odors. The eye gives up", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.text.ff96be", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "text", "filler": "Mind is one portion taken out of it, thoughts and", "span": "desires are its object, placed outside. \"Having by self-conscious knowledge", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.letter.5c4afd", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "letter", "filler": "'Our mind was absent,' they say, 'we did not perceive", "span": "any act.' Without self-consciousness the body does not make known", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.practice.22a45d", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "practice", "filler": "These ten objects (what is spoken, smelled, seen, felt) have", "span": "reference to self-consciousness; the ten subjects (speech, the senses, mind)", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.planet.e2a224", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "planet", "filler": "That future life is reached by two roads; one leading", "span": "to the world of Brahman (the conditioned), beyond which there", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.element.af7c1d", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "element", "filler": "The speculations on the fate of the soul after death", "span": "seem to have been peculiar to the royal families of", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.symbol.b456f2", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Men do and must [pg 190] listen to that as", "span": "to nothing else;\u2014all else is wind in comparison. From of", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.concept.6471b4", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "concept", "filler": "Leaving your friends, giving up honorable position; with a firm", "span": "purpose to obtain the joys of heaven, although you may", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.text.ff96be", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "text", "filler": "Whoever neglects right consideration about his present life, and because", "span": "he hopes to escape in the end, therefore disregards all", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.letter.5c4afd", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "letter", "filler": "A hare rescued from the serpent's mouth, would it go", "span": "back again to be devoured? holding a torch and burning", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.practice.22a45d", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "practice", "filler": "The root of mind (manas) is twofold, being both material,", "span": "and also intelligent; nature by its involutions is the cause,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.planet.e2a224", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "planet", "filler": "Thus not distinguishing aright, these are called excessive quibbles, marks", "span": "of folly, nature changes, and so on. To worship and", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.element.af7c1d", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "element", "filler": "In brief, perceiving no limits to this emptiness, there is", "span": "opened to the view boundless knowledge. Endowed with inward [pg", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.symbol.b456f2", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "symbol", "filler": "the soul of Kapila) being rendered pure, forthwith there is", "span": "true deliverance; but if we encounter a union of cause", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.concept.6471b4", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "concept", "filler": "There are those who warring against desire are still influenced", "span": "by desire; who whilst possessed of body, act as though", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.text.ff96be", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "text", "filler": "This fault of birth and death, once understood, then there", "span": "is clear and plain perception. Obtaining this clear perception, then", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.letter.5c4afd", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "letter", "filler": "If this is what they call the 'I,' then are", "span": "all things living, one\u2014for all have this unchanging self\u2014not perfected", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.practice.22a45d", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "practice", "filler": "The great sage, everywhere celebrated, was called Mah\u00e2 K\u00e2syapa. His", "span": "original faith was that \"body and soul are different,\" but", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.planet.e2a224", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "planet", "filler": "And now putting away forever covetous desire for such a", "span": "formless state of being, his restless heart was agitated still,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.element.af7c1d", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "element", "filler": "Rightly considering the world, we put away birth and old", "span": "age, disease and death; but now because we see that", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.symbol.b456f2", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Erroneous thoughts as to the joy of heaven are still", "span": "entwined by the fast cords of lust. The nobleman attending", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.concept.6471b4", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "concept", "filler": "Sorrow and joy spring up in all that lives, these", "span": "at least are not the works of Isvara; for if", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.veda_upanishad_pd.text.ff96be", "family_id": "veda_upanishad_pd", "role": "text", "filler": "The study of heretical books not leading to right thought,", "span": "causes the lustful heart to increase and grow, for these", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.andes_amazon.planet.d7d50f", "family_id": "andes_amazon", "role": "planet", "filler": "33 Cap. IX.\u2014En que trata c\u00f3mo Inca Yupanqui, despues de", "span": "haber desbaratado y muerto \u00e1 Uscovilca, tom\u00f3 sus vestidos y", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.andes_amazon.element.6f75e8", "family_id": "andes_amazon", "role": "element", "filler": "Y estos dos ans\u00ed despachados, dicen que \u00e9l ans\u00edmismo se", "span": "parti\u00f3 por el derecho h\u00e1cia el Cuzco, que es por", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.andes_amazon.symbol.93261e", "family_id": "andes_amazon", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Y la guaca de este Viracocha est\u00e1 en derecho desta", "span": "[p\u00e1g. 7] quemadura un tiro de piedra della, en un", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.andes_amazon.concept.9f6562", "family_id": "andes_amazon", "role": "concept", "filler": "Y porque este Viracocha all\u00ed se hubiese sentado, le hicieron", "span": "[p\u00e1g. 8] en aquel lugar una muy rica y suntuosa", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.andes_amazon.text.8b7710", "family_id": "andes_amazon", "role": "text", "filler": "Sali\u00f3 primero el que se llam\u00f3 Ayar Cache y su", "span": "mujer con \u00e9l, que se llam\u00f3 Mama Guaco; y tras", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.andes_amazon.letter.452ce5", "family_id": "andes_amazon", "role": "letter", "filler": "[p\u00e1g. 13] CAP. IV.\u2014En que trata c\u00f3mo Ayar Mango se", "span": "descendi\u00f3 de los altos de Guanacaure \u00e1 vivir \u00e1 otra", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.andes_amazon.practice.ce200b", "family_id": "andes_amazon", "role": "practice", "filler": "Y acabado de decir esto por el \u00eddolo Ayar Oche,", "span": "torn\u00f3se piedra ans\u00ed como estaba, con sus alas, y luego", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.andes_amazon.planet.d7d50f", "family_id": "andes_amazon", "role": "planet", "filler": "Y esto hecho, pasaron adelante Mango Capac y su gente,", "span": "y hablaron con Alcaviza, dici\u00e9ndole que el sol los inviaba", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
