{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "Accordingly, the honoring of the gods is a fundamental thing", "span": "in the Shinto thought and in the Japanese civilization and", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "The first Mikado, however, was not the real son of", "span": "Amaterasu , according to the mythic tradition of the prehistoric", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "Within this large enclosure are others of similar structure, all", "span": "made of the wood of cryptomeria trees, and left unpainted", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
