{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "[Pg 1] CHAPTER I. MATERIALS FOR THE STUDY OF SHINTO.", "span": "Prehistoric Shinto .--Ethnologists are agreed that the predominant element of", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "It is certain, however, that a considerable body of myth,", "span": "together with formal rituals, was already in existence, having been", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "It is preceded by a valuable introduction. Nihongi .--The mythical", "span": "narrative of the Nihongi , or 'Chronicles of Japan,' also", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "It contains little which is not also to be found", "span": "in these two works. Unlike them, the Kiujiki makes no", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
