{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "621; but there is little or no trace of it", "span": "in the older Shinto. For a long time there was", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "Moreover, as a social animal, he is prompted to communicate", "span": "his religious thoughts and feelings to his fellow men. Without", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "They stretched forth their hands and danced and sang together,", "span": "exclaiming, 'Oh! how delightful! how pleasant! how clear!'\" The Nihongi", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "It is probably connected with kaburu , to cover, and", "span": "has the general meaning of \"above,\" \"superior.\" Kami is the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "Conversely the combatant who is thrown down cannot further resist", "span": "without struggling against his own weight as well as against", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "[Pg 9] Moreover, not only human beings, but birds, beasts,", "span": "plants and trees, seas and mountains, and all other things", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "A recent [Pg 10] dictionary gives the following essentially modern", "span": "definitions of this word :-- Kami . 1. Something which", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "God = infinite power + absolute humanity. B. God =", "span": "absolute humanity + infinite power. But in the stage of", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "The doctrine of the conservation of energy is the physical", "span": "counterpart of the doctrine of the immortality of the soul.", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "The Zeus of Homer is an example. He is much", "span": "more the Father of Gods and men than a Sky", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "In Shinto it is the first of the two great", "span": "currents of religious thought with which we are chiefly concerned.", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "Different worshippers might give different answers. The habitual neglect by", "span": "the Japanese nation of the grammatical distinction between singular and", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "They are simply thought of as in some sort of", "span": "way living things. Mud and sand are dubbed Kami ,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "With the advance of social organization he is a chief", "span": "or a king. Sometimes in these metaphors we can trace", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Even a dog appreciates the distinction between a real rat", "span": "and the object which it pleases him to fancy one,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "The grammatical structure of their languages compels Europeans to say", "span": "either he or she in speaking of deities. In Japan", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "Tohe , another word for chieftain, occurs in the name", "span": "of the Wind-God, Shina tsu tohe. Nushi , master, is", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "Some of these are also nature deities. In others we", "span": "find a union of the two deity-making tendencies. Thus Koyane,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "Moreover, owing to the neglect by the Japanese of grammatical", "span": "forms indicating number, it is frequently hard to tell whether", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "There were no arts of sculpture or painting in Japan", "span": "before their introduction from China in historical times, and the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "It is with them not a matter of etiquette, but", "span": "of poverty of imagination, that power which, as Mr. P.", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Such beings, however, are not at first conceived of as", "span": "in any way incorporeal. [Pg 25] There is considerable confusion", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "Spiritism .--We now come to Stage IV., or spiritism. The", "span": "great and obvious difficulties connected with the anthropomorphic conception of", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "It therefore corresponds to the Shekinah (that which dwells) of", "span": "the Jews, and, though in a less marked degree, to", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "Tama next means something valuable, as a jewel. Then, as", "span": "jewels are mostly globular in shape, it has come to", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "Where dost thou now wish to dwell?' The spirit answered", "span": "and said: 'I wish to dwell on Mount Mimoro, in", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "It is a curious circumstance that in later times the", "span": "mitama par excellence were the phallic Sahe no Kami. Their", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "Mystery is not the vital element of religion. It depends", "span": "on what we know, not on what we [Pg 32]", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "The real God is his actual body; the mitama is", "span": "his divine spirit: the mitama-shiro (spirit-token) is the thing, be", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "Remaining there, it (the mitama) did good service in both", "span": "cases. These Gods, moreover, sometimes reveal their real bodies and", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "Hirata himself calls a stone idol the mitama of the", "span": "God, and speaks of the Sun-Goddess's mitama as going backward", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "The Japanese language has no word for vegetable except s\u014dmoku", "span": ", a recent compound of Chinese origin. The word for", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "The truth is that Shinto is derived in a much", "span": "less degree from the second of the two great currents", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "II. X, sometimes when alive, more frequently when dead, is", "span": "possessed of superhuman powers, usually borrowed from those of nature,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "The mere exaggeration of the human faculties may produce an", "span": "inferior [Pg 38] sort of deity, but no really great", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "612) is compared to the sun issuing from the clouds.", "span": "Tenshi , or \"Son of Heaven,\" a Chinese term freely", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "It may be objected that it is contrary to the", "span": "general law of human development to make the higher metaphorical", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "Herbert Spencer, in his 'Sociology,' says:-- \"There are proofs that", "span": "like confusion of metaphor with fact leads to Sun-worship. Complimentary", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "The deification of living Mikados was titular rather than real.", "span": "I am not aware that any specific so-called miraculous powers", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "There is nothing in these notices to show that divine", "span": "worship is intended. An oath made by Yemishi or Ainus,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "Under the name of Hachiman, the Mikado Ojin, visibly owing", "span": "to Chinese and Buddhist influences, became an important deity in", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "It is probable, however, that some of the numerous obscure", "span": "deities mentioned in the Kojiki and Nihongi are deified men.", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "He continued to live in his old thatched home upon", "span": "the hill, while his soul was being worshipped in the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "The modern Japanese, imbued with Chinese ideas, throw them back", "span": "into the old Shinto, and have persuaded themselves that it", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "The truth [Pg 46] is that only a very small", "span": "part of the Japanese nation knew, or pretended to know,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "Other nobles traced their lineage from, and paid a special", "span": "worship to, personages who never existed as individual human beings.", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "Of the cult of the Uji-gami as such we know", "span": "very little. The Kojiki mentions the fact of various deities", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "Wrestlers worship Nomi no Sukune, who was probably a real", "span": "person, and Chinese doctors the legendary Chinese Emperor Shinnung. Confucian", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "Yamato-dake's mitama is in one place said to have been", "span": "changed into a white bird. Of the mitama of ordinary", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Even now the bakemono , though differing little from our", "span": "ghost, is quite distinct from the human mitama or tamashi\u00ef", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "It is everywhere in the lower culture conceived of as", "span": "material, though capable of changing its form and appearance without", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "Mi-kage , or \"august shadow,\" is an ancient synonym for", "span": "mi-tama . It is unnecessary to suppose that anything but", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "He does open it, upon which his life or soul", "span": "comes out and flies away like a white cloud to", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "All men have ki (breath), kei (form), and sei (life).", "span": "The kon rules the ki and the sei . The", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "The Kojiki , after relating the death and burial of", "span": "Izanami on Mount Hiba, at the boundary of the Land", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "How can it be said that the dead have no", "span": "knowledge?'\" Evidently at this time there were two opinions on", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "His palace fronts the south. Immediately after death corpses are", "span": "laid with the head to the north, a position scrupulously", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "3, 7th month, 6th day. The Empress Hibasu-hime no Mikoto", "span": "died. Some time before the burial, the Emperor commanded his", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "His original title was therefore changed, and he was called", "span": "Hashi no Omi. This was how it came to pass", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "An ode in the 'Sheking' laments the death of three", "span": "brothers who were sacrificed at the funeral of Duke Muh,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "This, although poetry, no doubt represents a real belief. Mr.", "span": "Andrew Lang mentions the case of an Irish peasant woman,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "Several of the pseudo-ancestors are in reality deified types, analogous", "span": "to such conceptions as Tommy Atkins or Mrs. Grundy. As", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "It was a personified human abstraction--namely, Psyche, who was described", "span": "by Keats as The latest born and loveliest by far", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "The wani , or sea-monster, belongs to the sea-God, and", "span": "the dragon belongs to (or is) Taka okami (the rain-God).", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "Tattooing, which some have associated with this form of belief,", "span": "existed as a means of distinguishing rank and occupation. The", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "Any God may send an earthquake or a pestilence. In", "span": "853 there was a great epidemic of smallpox. An oracle", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "But this conception requires a greater amount of scientific knowledge", "span": "than the ancient Japanese possessed. They had necessarily only imperfect", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "We may be sure that the Ephesians would have resented", "span": "any attempt to identify their Diana with that of other", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "Another cause of multiplication is the mistake of supposing the", "span": "same deity with different epithets to be different Gods. In", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "It is this last, the most usual fate of polytheisms,", "span": "which threatens the old Gods of Japan. Weakened by the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "He eventually split up, first into two, then into a", "span": "group of deities, and finally became almost wholly neglected. The", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "The men of that time made a song, saying: Udzumasa", "span": "Has executed The God of the Everlasting World Who we", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "The shintai in some respects resembles the Greek \u03ac\u03b3\u03b1\u03bb\u03bc\u03ac .", "span": "Both were originally offerings which became tokens of the God's", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "[44] Some serve as milestones, and some are erected at", "span": "the outskirts of villages to keep away the demon small-pox.", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "Another sword, called Kusanagi, has been worshipped for centuries at", "span": "Atsuta, near Nagoya. It was this sword which Susa no", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "There is no more harm in representing a God, pictorially", "span": "or in sculpture, as an old man than there is", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "His childish imagination was stirred by an instinctive impulse, to", "span": "be compared with that which prompts the gambolling of a", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "And even when a language has acquired some capacity for", "span": "the direct expression of spiritual facts, it is found that", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "He comes, and his heralds run before him, and touch", "span": "the leaves of oaks and planes and beeches lucid green", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "There have always been literal-minded unbelievers, who reject the myth", "span": "and its religious contents without discrimination, and simply value it,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "For such, I take it, is the real meaning of", "span": "the story by which the Mikados are feigned to be", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "Some go so far as to say that ritual is", "span": "the source of all religious myth. The late Mr. D.", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "The worship of the Sun is assuredly not the outcome,", "span": "but the source, of the Japanese solar myths, though it", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "Thereafter divine beings were produced between them.\" Pfleiderer says: [53]", "span": "\"There is not unfrequently found in [Pg 85] the mythology", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "The same authority gives Kuni-toko-tachi a place lower down in", "span": "the genealogical table. The Kiujiki has a first God called", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "Several of them, however, show that the divinely mysterious process", "span": "of growth, so all-important to an agricultural nation, had attracted", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "We have therefore three distinct conceptions of creation in Japanese", "span": "myth--first as generation in the most literal sense, second, as", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "The tama-boko no michi would then mean \"the road where", "span": "phallic symbols are set up.\" There is abundant evidence that", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "Herbert Spencer [61] has shown how universally the spear has", "span": "this meaning. Britannia's trident is a familiar example. Theseus, in", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "Suppose that we supplement that which is [Pg 90] incomplete", "span": "in thee with that which is superfluous in me, and", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "In the case of Shinto shrines, it is called the", "span": "Nakago no mibashira (central august pillar), and in ordinary houses", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "The author of the myth of the Sun-Goddess endeavours to", "span": "smooth over the difficulty of her conjugal relations with her", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "The last deity to be produced was the God of", "span": "Fire, Kagu-tsuchi, also called Ho-musubi (fire-growth). In giving birth to", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "Her body was already putrid, maggots swarmed over it, and", "span": "the eight thunder-gods had been generated in her various members.", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "Moreover, he threw down his girdle, which was called Nagachiha", "span": "no Kami. Moreover, he threw down his upper garment, which", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "Grimm, in his 'Teutonic Mythology,' says that \"to Death is", "span": "ascribed a highway levelled, smooth, and kept in repair, on", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "Heaven and earth were still \"not far separated.\" Ame no", "span": "mi-hashira (Heaven-august-pillar) is one of the names of the Wind-God.", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "Lustration is a wide-world practice, [71] and the myth was", "span": "clearly suggested by it, not vice vers\u00e2 . Izanagi's career", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "They figure largely in the Sh\u00f4jiroku genealogies of Japanese noble", "span": "families. Through one of them, named Masa-ya-a-katsu-kachi-haya-hi-ama-no-oshi-ho-mi-mi, the Mikados trace", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "By the advice of Omohi-kane no Mikoto (the Thought-combiner or", "span": "Counsellor deity) the long-singing birds of the Eternal Land (cocks)", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "Finally Ame no Koyane, the ancestor of the Nakatomi, recited", "span": "his Oho-harahi or \"Great purification\" liturgy. The above episode is", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "A Japanese baby knows that these are simply the numerals", "span": "from one to ten. But they have given much trouble", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "This is not the only attempt of myth-makers to account", "span": "for the aloofness maintained by these two deities. The same", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "In certain stages of civilization, sacrifices of the kind are", "span": "practised, and are frequently offered to water-spirits conceived in animal", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "Ohonamochi's eighty brothers went to pay court to a female", "span": "deity named Yakami-hime, taking him with them as porter \"to", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Again, on the night of the next day, he was", "span": "put into the centipede and wasp chamber; but as his", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "Ohonamochi then took hold of the hair of the Great", "span": "Deity and tied it to the rafters of the chamber.", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "\" He was assisted in doing so by a dwarf", "span": "deity called Sukuna-bikona, who wore garments of bird skins and", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "They sent down several other deities to prepare the world", "span": "for the advent of Ninigi, a grandchild of the Sun-Goddess,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "This arrow, when it fell, hit Ame-waka-hiko on the top", "span": "of his breast. At this time Ame-waka-hiko was lying down", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "Therefore again I issue my commands to thee more circumstantially,", "span": "that is to say: Let the public matters which thou", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "Therefore Futsunushi no Kami appointed Kunado no Kami as guide,", "span": "and went on a circuit of pacification. Any who were", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Moreover, a light shines from his mouth and from his", "span": "posteriors. His eye-balls are like an eight-hand mirror, and have", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "This was still the practice in the island of Hachij\u014d", "span": "in 1878, and even in Japan no longer than a", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "[Pg 115] The child thus born was the father of", "span": "Jimmu Tenno, the first human sovereign of Japan. Hohodemi's troubles", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "A comparatively advanced civilization is indicated by the sword and", "span": "fish-hooks forged of iron (the Homeric fish-hook was of horn).", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "Now I have heard from the old sea-father that in", "span": "the east there is a fair land encircled by blue", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "Then sacrificing to the Gods of Heaven and Earth, and", "span": "bringing on our backs the might of the Sun-Goddess, let", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "Thereupon Take-mika-tsuchi no Kami addressed Takakuraji, saying: 'My sword, which", "span": "is called Futsu no Mitama, I will now place in", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Again he made a vow, saying:-- \"' I will now", "span": "take the sacred jars and sink them in the River", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "His name and that of his son appear very frequently", "span": "in the Sh\u00f4jiroku genealogies. Jimmu took to wife a daughter", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "Among these the light and warmth of the Sun and", "span": "the sources of their daily food held the chief place.", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "No form of faith is so odious--because of the danger", "span": "of relapse--as that from which we have emerged with painful", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "The same is the case with Mikoto , which corresponds", "span": "roughly to our \"majesty.\" Of course Japan is not the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "Her most usual appellation is Ama terasu no Oho-kami, or", "span": "the [Pg 125] Heaven-shining-great-deity. She is also called Ama-terasu hiru-me,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "Moreover, that there having been an omen of a crane", "span": "which alighted on the arsenal of the Government House, the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "\"Under these circumstances, we (the names of the envoys follow)", "span": "present these great offerings by the hands of Komaye, Imbe", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "\"Declared with deep reverence.\" The solar character of Ama-terasu or", "span": "Tensh\u014ddaijin having become obscured, the people have personified the Sun", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "I have seen the eastern wall of a private courtyard", "span": "which was pierced with a round hole for the convenience", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "I am disposed to regard this personage as the Sun-deity", "span": "of the earlier Yamato Japanese, from whom their chieftains were", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "There is a recognition of her beneficent character in the", "span": "joy of Gods and men when she emerged from the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "Hiru-ko is written with Chinese characters, which mean \"leech-child\"; and", "span": "it is stated that when this God had completed his", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "He is reckoned one of the seven Gods of good", "span": "fortune, and is a favourite deity to pray to for", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Yet I have before me a 'History of the Empire", "span": "of Japan,' compiled by doctors of the Imperial University, and", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "The Nihongi says, under the date b.c. 92:-- [Pg 135]", "span": "\" Before this the two Gods Ama-terasu no Oho-kami and", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "The Sun-Goddess in her capacity as sovereign is attended by", "span": "a Court of minor deities who belong to the class", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "[103] There is a God called Ame no hi-washi (heaven-sun-eagle),", "span": "which, although not to be identified with the yatagarasu ,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "Torrent Goddesses are born from the fragments of his sword.", "span": "He breaks down the divisions between the rice-fields and defiles", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "Dr. Florenz summarily rejects Hirata's theory that Susa no wo", "span": "is identical with the Moon-God Tsuki-yomi. It must be admitted", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "A Many\u014dshiu poem calls the moon Sasurahe-otoko, that is to", "span": "say, the banished or vagabond youth. All this establishes a", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Several of Susa no wo's acts have an unmistakably beneficent", "span": "character, as his rescue of Inada hime, and his provision", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "Their feet beat time to a wildly shouted chorus, and", "span": "they sweep along wholly regardless of obstacles or collisions.\" The", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "The usual derivation of his name is from tsuki ,", "span": "moon, and yomi , darkness. It is to be observed,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "The scarecrow is regarded as a sort of deity. He", "span": "is said to know everything in the empire, though he", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "The simplest of all is the ji-matsuri , or ji-chin-sai", "span": "(earth-festival or earth-calming-festival), which is the ceremony of propitiating the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "Iku-dama , which has the same meaning, is a contraction", "span": "for iku kuni-dama . Moto\u00f6ri says that any God who", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "He could assume the form of a snake or of", "span": "a human being. The name Ohonamochi tells us nothing. It", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Miwa, in Yamato, was another seat of this deity's worship.", "span": "To be more exact, it was his nigi-tama , or", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "He mentions a practice by persons whose friends were absent", "span": "on pilgrimages of making a model of a house with", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "In a.d. 684 there was a great earthquake, and a", "span": "new island was formed at Idzu. A drumming sound was", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "The drying up or overflowing of a lake within its", "span": "crater was supposed to portend famine, pestilence, drought, or the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "Mountain Class-Deities .--The Kojiki and Nihongi mention a Mountain-God or", "span": "Gods, [118] called Yama tsu mi (mountain-body), as among the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "In Japanese myth the serpent or dragon is almost always", "span": "associated with water in some of its forms. We also", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "There is a superstition at the present day that the", "span": "mouths and pools of rivers are haunted by monsters called", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Well-Gods .--Sacred wells are known in Japan. They are called", "span": "mi-wi (august well) or mana-wi (true well). There is one", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "Wind-Gods .--The Nihongi speaks of one Wind-God named Shinatsu-hiko (wind-long-prince).", "span": "He was produced from Izanagi's breath when he puffed away", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "Indeed Hirata argues that they are one and the same", "span": "deity. He points out that Futsunushi is not mentioned in", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "3. Futsu is the regular Japanese phonetic equivalent of the", "span": "Korean pul , \"fire.\" In Furu-no mitama and Furu-musubi (for", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "It is probably as a war-god that he was constituted", "span": "the Ujigami of the arrow-makers, and that offerings of horses", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "There are numerous shrines to this deity. By the Ika-dzuchi,", "span": "which were generated from the putrefying corpse of Izanami, we", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "So at last the ships were built.\" Other Fire-Gods .--Futsunushi's", "span": "quality as a Fire-God had been quite forgotten even in", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Furnace Gods .--Along with the Gods of Fire we may", "span": "place the deities of the domestic cooking furnace, namely Kamado", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "Ukemochi (the Food Goddess) .--Cicero, in his treatise 'De Natura", "span": "Deorum,' asks whether any one is mad enough to believe", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "In a work of the eighth century the Sun-Goddess is", "span": "said to have appeared to the Mikado Y\u016briaku in a", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "The parentage of the Food-Goddess is variously given in different", "span": "myths. One story makes her the daughter of Izanagi and", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "But, as so often happens, the functions of this God", "span": "have been enlarged so as to make him a sort", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "Klaproth finds in Japanese books that \"the people in Japan", "span": "worship the inari (fox) as a tutelar God: little temples", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "It is emphasized by the ancient custom of the Mikado", "span": "tilling land in person, and by the Miko at Kasuga", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "A case is recorded in which this was done for", "span": "the sake of protection to the bearers. The sacred tree", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "ye trees, bud! or I will [Pg 166] strip you", "span": "of your bark.\" Brand's 'Popular Antiquities of Britain' records several", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "These are class-deities. Kaya nu hime .--The deity of herbs", "span": "and grasses is called Kaya nu hime (reed-lady), or Nu-dzuchi", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "No doubt each household had also its Yabune no Kami.", "span": "Hirata, in his Tamadasuki , gives a prayer to this", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "All this shows that the original identity of demons and", "span": "diseases has not yet been wholly lost sight of in", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "Whether the Gate-divinity is one or several does not trouble", "span": "them. 2. GODS OF ABSTRACTIONS. Izanagi and Izanami .--The conspicuous", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "Last of all was composed the philosophic proem with which", "span": "the book opens. Izanagi and Izanami belong to that stage", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "The Wind-God was his breath and the Gods of Water", "span": "and Clay were formed of the urine and f\u0153ces of", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "There is, however, a modicum of truth in this writer's", "span": "statement. Though not the first sentient beings, Izanagi and Izanami", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "I am disposed to prefer the derivation which takes Iza", "span": "as the name of a place. The Nihongi mentions a", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "Musuko , a boy, and musume , a girl, contain", "span": "the same element. As a God's name, Musubi is usually", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "The same author points out the resemblance of this God", "span": "to the Hindu Siva, who represents the fructifying principle, the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "This is possibly the beginning of the official worship of", "span": "this God. In 859 several Musubi deities were raised to", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "He is barely mentioned in myth, and his cult, which", "span": "is comparatively modern, was no doubt, as Hirata suggests, a", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Take-minakata , the deity of Suha in Shinano, may be", "span": "a real ancestral deity. He is very popular at the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "His origin is really unknown, but he is placed provisionally", "span": "among deified human beings in accordance with the accepted tradition", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "In several of these he calls himself Bosatsu (Bodhisattwa), which", "span": "is a Buddhist term something like our saint. He is", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "Sad to say, there is no book in which the", "span": "real facts have been set down after investigation. \" The", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "On his departure he addressed the following lines to a", "span": "plum tree in his garden:-- When the east wind [149]", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "Then the Minister of State Kintada died suddenly. Three days", "span": "after, he came alive again, and informed the Mikado that", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "But I will give help to those who piously express", "span": "their sorrow.\" Eight persons who were present took down this", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "No doubt the authors found these things in their materials,", "span": "and were loth to excise edifying incidents, however badly they", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "There were Be of weavers, of farmers, of potters, &c.,", "span": "a Be for the supply of necessaries to the Palace,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "The Imi-be, [152] his reputed descendants, discharged a number of", "span": "duties connected with the State religious ceremonies, including the provision", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "A few of these are nature-deities. Of the remainder some", "span": "may be deified real men, but I prefer to reckon", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "In the Many\u00f4shiu he is called upon by a lover", "span": "to [Pg 186] punish him if he is insincere in", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "In Japan, the phallus symbolizes two distinct, although not unrelated,", "span": "principles. Primarily, it represents the generative or procreative power, and", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "The deification of these symbols came later. In the norito", "span": "entitled Michiahe [156] there are three Sahe no kami, namely,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Thus in 735, during an epidemic, the Governor of Dazaifu", "span": "in Kiushiu was ordered to celebrate a michi-ahe , or", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "Its shape, formed of Izanagi's staff, is consistent with this", "span": "view. In the Tsujiura, or Cross Roads divination, this God", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "I have more than a suspicion that the efficacy of", "span": "rice for this purpose, and also of the beans used", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "He gives a drawing of the sticks used for the", "span": "purpose, of the phallic character of which there can be", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "[Pg 192] [Pg 193] Fire, kindled from kedzurikake after prayer,", "span": "was given out to the people by the priests of", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "The gruel partaken of at the Sahe no Kami festival", "span": "on the 15th of the 1st month was made of", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "The potency of red as a charm against small-pox is", "span": "not unknown to European folk-lore. Phalli are coloured a bright", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Their answer was that it was a very ancient custom.", "span": "They were called Sai no kami, [164] and were made", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "At this time the child of Mi-toshi no Kami (august-harvest-god)", "span": "went to that rice-field and spat upon the food, after", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "Primarily they were symbols, next objects of magic. Finally Religion", "span": "intervened, and by her handmaids Personification and Myth raised them", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "The Sahe no Kami were the mitama par excellence .", "span": "They were also called tamuke no Kami (Gods of offerings)", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "[171] Oni .-- Oni , or demons, have no individual", "span": "names. It is clear from the Kojiki and Nihongi mythical", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "The very terrible deity known as Bimb\u014d-gami, the God of", "span": "Poverty, is of later origin. [Pg 200] CHAPTER IX. THE", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "Thus a Sun-worship Be, or hereditary corporation, was established in", "span": "577. One version of the myth of Ohonamochi represents him", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "In the Jimmu legend there is mention of the appointment", "span": "of a Michi no Omi (minister of the way) as", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "It was presided over by an official called Haku. He", "span": "had the supreme control of all the Shinto State ceremonies,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "When they are fortunate, they make him presents, but if", "span": "they are ill, or meet with disaster, they set it", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "Saishu .--The high-priest at Ise was called Saishu, or worship-master.", "span": "This office was hereditary in the Fujinami family, a branch", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "No special education is necessary for the discharge of the", "span": "duties of a Kannushi, which consist in the recital of", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "They will not use the same fire for cooking as", "span": "other people. Miyakko .--The hereditary chief priests of Kitsuki in", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "They were young girls attached to all the principal shrines", "span": "for the performance of the kagura dances, and cooking the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "These are modern institutions. Kamube .--The peasants who tilled the", "span": "glebe lands of the shrine and their place of residence", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "No doubt he honours the dead in this way as", "span": "well as the living. But the occasions for the worship", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "The Nihongi [176] states that the Ministers clapped hands in", "span": "honour of the Empress when she ascended the throne. More", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "There are always worshippers who well know that the God", "span": "does not eat the food, drink the wine, or wear", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "Symbolic gifts are, of course, not confined to religion. In", "span": "ancient Greece a gift of earth and water indicated a", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "There are several cases in the norito where they [Pg", "span": "212] are made by way of reward for their services", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "Under food are included rice, in ear and in grain,", "span": "hulled and in husk, rice cakes, fruit, sea-ear, shell-fish, vegetables,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "[Pg 214] Clothing .--The clothing of the ancient Japanese consisted", "span": "of hemp, yuju (a fibre made of the inner bark", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "The paper slips represent the yufu , or mulberry-bark fibre.", "span": "The use of yufu for clothing having become more or", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "Tama-gushi are often mentioned. I take it that in this", "span": "combination tama means gift or offering, not spirit or jewel,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "Hepburn's Japanese dictionary knows no other. It is illustrated by", "span": "the fact that instead of the worshipper bringing gohei to", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "Jewels occur sometimes in the lists of Shinto offerings. Mirrors", "span": ".--The ancient Japanese mirrors did not greatly differ from those", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "One which was stolen by a thief is said to", "span": "have left him and returned to the treasury of its", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "Cases are also recorded of men being buried alive in", "span": "the foundations of a bridge, a castle, or an artificial", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "They wash and purify him, and make him put on", "span": "pure clothing. He is then brought before the God. A", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "There is some difficulty in applying the principle of substitution", "span": "for an actual human sacrifice to a custom which was", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "At the festivals of Gion and Hachiman men riding on", "span": "hobby-horses ( koma-gata ) or with a wooden horse's head", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "The Japanese words for shrine indicate that it is intended", "span": "as a house for the God. Miya , august house,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "Even the great shrines of Ise ( pp. 228, 229", "span": ") are of no great size and of purposely plain", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "Many minor shrines existed in all parts of the country.", "span": "The shrines are classed as great and small, the respective", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "The medi\u00e6val Shintoists identified him with Susa no wo. More", "span": "recently it has been declared officially that he is really", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "God or Gods Worshipped . Gion. Yamashiro. Susa no wo.", "span": "The number was finally raised to twenty-two in 1039 by", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "When introduced into Japan at some unknown date (the Kojiki", "span": "and Nihongi do not mention them) the Japanese called them", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "They contain petitions for rain in time of drought, good", "span": "harvests, preservation from earthquake and conflagration, children, health and long", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "The Mongol invasion was notified to Ise in 1277 with", "span": "the happiest results. The Yengishiki contains no norito addressed to", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "The commonly received opinion that the latter indicate a belief", "span": "in a future state is, perhaps, after all, erroneous. Nor", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "Sometimes the prayer is written out on paper and deposited", "span": "in the shrine, perhaps accompanied by the petitioner's hair or", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "Therefore, sitting on a rock, I make this solemn declaration", "span": "of alliance.\" A curse pronounced over a well in 456", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "This practice became systematized in the period 749-757, and was", "span": "very prevalent for several centuries longer. A rain of volcanic", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "Uzume's dance before the cave to which the Sun-Goddess had", "span": "retired is supposed to be its prototype. Important shrines have", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "Intending pilgrims associate themselves in clubs called K\u014d , whose", "span": "members each contribute five sen a month to the pilgrimage", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "This is called em-pai , or distant worship. Special shrines", "span": "are provided in some places where the God will accept", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "Morals .--Before proceeding to examine the relation of morals to", "span": "religion in Shinto, let us note some general considerations. Right", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "There is, however, a tendency for these motives to encroach", "span": "on each other's provinces without relinquishing their own. Acts which", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "[194] Incest, bestiality, wounding, witchcraft, and [Pg 243] certain interferences", "span": "with agricultural operations are the only offences against the moral", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "25-220), says that \"the wives and children of those who", "span": "break the laws are confiscated, and for grave crimes the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "In the same year laws were promulgated dealing with dishonesty,", "span": "retaining slaves belonging to other people, bringing plaints of adultery", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "It was indeed the power of the ruler which held", "span": "the community together, but the idea of the society being", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "Indeed we could scarcely expect to find such offences noticed", "span": "in it, as the application of the criminal law in", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "For the offences of the nation generally, which it was", "span": "the main object of the Ohoharahi to absolve, no punishment", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "This is one offence. Thou didst wrongfully take them, comprising", "span": "them in the Cart-keepers' Be after they had been allotted", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "The Ohoharahi includes the committing of nuisances among the offences", "span": "to be absolved by it. Sexual Immorality and Uncleanness .--It", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Those shameless wights Yajir\u014d and Kidahachi, the heroes of the", "span": "Hizakurige , were troubled with scruples in this matter, which", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "The prohibition of unions between brothers and sisters by the", "span": "mother's side--that is, practically of the full blood--and not of", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "As in the Mosaic law, menstruation and child-birth were regarded", "span": "as sources of uncleanness. [201] The custom of providing a", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "In 801 a Great Purification ceremony was performed, because a", "span": "dead dog had been discovered under one of the palace", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "If he has vomited or passed blood, he must not", "span": "worship for two days, if he has an abscess, until", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "647 was certainly due to Buddhist influences. The first hint", "span": "that it was offensive to the Shinto Gods to eat", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "Whereas in ancient times the Mikados ate the flesh of", "span": "deer and wild boar as ha-gatame (hardening the teeth) on", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "A separate place was assigned them for their prayers. Other", "span": "words of ill omen were \"death,\" for which \"recovery\" was", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "The intending officiator or worshipper remained indoors ( i-gomori ),", "span": "abstained from speech and noise, and ate food cooked at", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "In 463 the Mikado Y\u016briaku desired to see the form", "span": "of the deity of Mimuro, and ordered one of his", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "It is frequently mentioned in the old Japanese traditions. The", "span": "Kojiki says that the God Kushiyadama was appointed steward for", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "A modern Japanese writer, describing a festival celebrated at Gion", "span": "in Ki\u00f4to on the last day of the year, says:", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "The need-fire, made by striking flints or by the fire-drill,", "span": "and used to rekindle all household fires, is one of", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "Misogi means \"body-sprinkling,\" and harahi is probably the same word", "span": "as arahi , \"wash.\" [212] Penitence is not one of", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "In the Izanagi myth a God of the Spittle (Haya-tama", "span": "no wo) is the result of that [Pg 261] deity's", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "As a religious practice, breathing away impurity is exemplified by", "span": "the custom of the Mikado breathing on certain aga mono", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "Susa no wo is said to have expiated his offences", "span": "by the loss of his hair and of his finger", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "A few days before, the parishioners and other believers who", "span": "wish to be purified go to the shrine and obtain", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "It is thought that evil spirits are diverted into these", "span": "images from the infant. It is an obvious degradation of", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "[Pg 265] The virtue of set forms of speech in", "span": "absolving from uncleanness is fully recognized in Shinto, as will", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "He thereafter partook of it along with the nation. Thus", "span": "the people learnt that the grain which they eat is", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "These officers on arriving at the yuki or suki district", "span": "performed a purification ceremony in presence of the local officials", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "The surrounding fence was made of brushwood and the gates", "span": "consisted of hurdles. Offerings having been made to the eight", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "Therefore, on behalf of the Sovran Grandchild, who will rule", "span": "peacefully and serenely for one thousand autumns and five hundred", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "The Brewer-maidens then with a pure mattock turned the first", "span": "sod and dug the holes for the four corner posts.", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "The preparation of the sake for the ceremony was preceded", "span": "by worship of the Well-God, the Furnace-God, and [Pg 273]", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "Moreover, whatever faults there be, receive these offerings with divine", "span": "amendment, with great amendment.\" The Mikado then bowed his head", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "Thereafter I did worship to the Sovran Gods who dwell", "span": "in the one hundred and eighty-six shrines.' \" Then, as", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "[232] Thereupon the Sovran dear divine ancestor and ancestress (of", "span": "the Mikado?) [Pg 276] gave command, saying: 'Do thou Hohi", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "\" The offerings were sixty jewels, white, red, and green,", "span": "a sword with mountings of gold and silver, a mirror,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "It appears from allusions in poetry and legend that there", "span": "was also a household Nihi-name. It was celebrated with closed", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "Kan-name (divine-tasting).--This was another harvest festival, distinguished from the preceding", "span": "by being celebrated in the ninth month, and being confined", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
