{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Then, celestial counsel having been held, they put to silence", "span": "the rock-roots and tree-roots, even to the smallest blades of", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "I humbly praise your honoured names, to wit, Yabune Kukunochi", "span": "no Mikoto and Yabune Toyo-uke hime no Mikoto [ House-tree", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "They consisted of rice, cakes, paper, cloth, egg-plant, fish, shellfish,", "span": "&c. Twice a year Kagura was performed. The ceremonies used", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
