{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "In the main a form of the northern branch of", "span": "Buddhism, it found its way originally to Japan vi\u00e2 Tibet,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "Its doctrines of sin and repentance, of fate, of future", "span": "bliss and woe, its profound metaphysics, and, perhaps more than", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Gy\u014dgi spent seven days and seven nights in prayer under", "span": "a tree close to the gate of the shrine, and", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "The principal founder of Ry\u014dbu was the famous (and fabulous)", "span": "K\u014db\u014d Daishi (died 835), to whom the invention of the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "[333] But Shinto, Buddhism of various sects, Confucianism, and Sung", "span": "philosophy constituted a very refractory mass of material, and the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "All these sects were much given to strained analogies and", "span": "fanciful comparisons in support of their views. The conversion of", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "The mode of imperial burial was modified in accordance with", "span": "Buddhist ideas of the worthlessness of these mortal frames of", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "The latter are an Indian conceit. They were originally set", "span": "up at cemeteries [Pg 365] in order to frighten wild", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "[Pg 366] [Pg 367] Still there were a few exceptions", "span": "to the general decay. At the two great shrines of", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "In some, Heaven-and-Earth is recognized as a sort of pantheistic", "span": "deity, distinct from the physical universe. Here we have Chinese", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "An oracle of Hachiman:-- I refuse the offerings of the", "span": "impure of heart. Some Gods are great, some small, some", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "Oracle of Temman tenjin , the deified Minister Sugahara no", "span": "Michizane [339] :-- All ye who come before me hoping", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "Receive the just commands of the Gods. Regard Heaven as", "span": "your father, Earth as your mother, and all things as", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "A son of a Mikado received the following inspiration in", "span": "a dream:-- It is the upright heart of all men", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "If there be any who, having studied the books of", "span": "China or practised the teachings of India, despise the instructions", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "The Samurai, or governing caste of the nation, devoted themselves", "span": "to these studies with amazing zeal and enthusiasm, to the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "He seems to have been wholly blind to the fact", "span": "that the exotic faiths and philosophies, whose intrusion into Shinto", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "He tacitly accepts the moral code of China, while protesting", "span": "that such things are unnecessary, as we are endowed by", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "Her religion owes much to the Shingaku and Ry\u014dbu doctrines.", "span": "While professing to worship Kunitokotachi, Izanagi, Izanami, and seven other", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "The followers of Shimamura call her an ikigami (live God),", "span": "and regard her as identical with the My\u00f4h\u00f4. How often", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "The reverence paid to the Mikado is not devoid of", "span": "a religious quality which has its source in Shinto. But", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
