{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "[232] It is to be understood that after he had", "span": "enshrined his nigi-tama , or gentle spirit, in Yamato, Ohonamochi", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "[255] Usually said to be Taka-musubi, Kamu-musubi, and the Sun-Goddess.", "span": "[256] Ninigi. [257] Poetical expressions for Japan. [258] That is,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "In the norito the further step is taken of recognizing", "span": "the same acts, committed on earth, as offences not only", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "676): \"The Mikado commanded, saying: 'Let a Great Purification (Oho-harahi)", "span": "be held in all quarters. The articles needed for this", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "It seems here to typify the attentive attitude of the", "span": "audience, or perhaps of the deities concerned. [272] Harahi-zare .", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "313. [282] That is, died. [283] What was the God", "span": "of Fire in the previous sentence is here simply \"Fire.\"", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Dr. Tylor, in his 'Primitive Culture,' i. 113, has noted", "span": "the tendency to attribute magical powers to pariahs and foreigners.", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "194. [317] 'Sociology,' i. 154. [318] See Mr. P. Lowell's", "span": "'Occult Japan,' p. 36. [319] Kannushi . [320] Saniha (pure", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "No inference can be drawn from the circumstance that Sun-worship", "span": "is common to them with many North-Asiatic races. The Sun", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "If the Malay or Polynesian element, which some have recognised", "span": "in the Japanese race, has any existence, it has left", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "For the ritual of Shinto our chief source of information", "span": "is the Yengishiki , a compilation made early in the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "The Kami are high, swift, good, rich, living, but not", "span": "infinite, omnipotent, or omniscient. Most of them had a father", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "The term Kami is applied in the Nihongi and Many\u014dshiu", "span": "to the tiger and the wolf. Izanagi gave to the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "He provides trees for the use of humanity, and rescues", "span": "a maiden from being devoured by a great serpent. 8", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "It is quite true that there is a large element", "span": "of ancestor worship in modern Japanese religious practices, but a", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "A deity of any class may become an Ujigami, and", "span": "there have been cases of a Buddha attaining to this", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "The Empress Jing\u014d, the legendary conqueror of Korea, also received", "span": "divine honours. At the present day, solemn services are held", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "At a still more recent stage\u2014though not in the old", "span": "records\u2014she becomes an independent personage who rules the Sun, while", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "Different gods are identified with one another, or the same", "span": "deities may be split up like Musubi into a pair,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "This implies a more or less spiritual conception of their", "span": "nature. Sometimes we hear of two mitama , one of", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "A brother of Jimmu Tenno, the first Mikado, is said", "span": "to have gone to the \u2018Eternal Land\u2019 at his death,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "As we have seen above, the Sun-goddess does not confine", "span": "herself to her function as a giver of light and", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "There are, however, two leading ideas by which Japanese myth", "span": "is redeemed from summary condemnation as a mere farrago of", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "The creation of mankind generally is not accounted for; but", "span": "the origin of many of the ruling caste is ascribed", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "The Nihongi tells us that\u2014 \u2018Izanagi and Izanami stood on", "span": "the floating bridge of Heaven (the rainbow) and held counsel", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "I have met a lovely youth.\u201d Izanagi then said, \u201cHow", "span": "delightful! I have met a lovely maiden.\u201d Afterwards he said,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "A third child, Susa no wo, the boisterous and unruly", "span": "Rain-storm god, was produced at the same time. When Izanami", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "All the mountains and rivers shook, and every land and", "span": "country quaked as he passed upwards. Amaterasu, in alarm, armed", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "\u2018The voices of the evil deities were like unto the", "span": "flies in the fifth moon as they swarmed, and a", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "But a different version ascribes this crime to the Moon-god,", "span": "and gives it as the reason why the 27 Sun-goddess", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "Ohonamochi. \u2014One of Susa no wo\u2019s children was an Earth-god", "span": "named Ohonamochi (great-name-possessor), who is at this day a very", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "The institution of the Hayato as Imperial Guards belongs to", "span": "a period not very long antecedent to the date of", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "35 CHAPTER IV THE GODS Nature-Gods of Individuals and of", "span": "Classes Some of the principal gods have already been introduced", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "In some myths she has a formidable rival in Taka", "span": "musubi , a god of Growth. The ascription of the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "It is kept in a bag of brocade which is", "span": "never opened or repaired, a new one being added on", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
