{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "Mr. B. H. Chamberlain translates by \u2018the Impetuous Male,\u2019 and", "span": "he may be correct. But there is a town in", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "With Ohonamochi there is associated his minister, an important deity", "span": "named Kotoshiro-nushi, and a dwarf-god, Sukuna-bikona, who is credited with", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "Another Sea-god, Toyotama hiko, has been already mentioned above (p.", "span": "31). River-Gods are represented as dragons or serpents. The resemblance", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "The name of the former is frequently written with Chinese", "span": "characters which imply that he is a Thunder-god, and Futsunushi", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "Both in ancient and modern times the domestic cooking-furnace has", "span": "been considered as a deity. Ukemochi , the Food-goddess, is", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Other sacred trees are not themselves gods, but 46 only", "span": "offerings to the deities before whose shrines they are planted.", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "Their names are supposed to be connected with a verb,", "span": "izanafu , to invite, and to refer to their mutual", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "Take-minakata , the god of Suha, in the province of", "span": "Shinano, may be a deity of this class. He was", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "Temmangu , the God of Learning and Caligraphy. If we", "span": "pass over the honours paid to 50 living and dead", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "\u2014In the Kojiki and Nihongi, a sort of titular divinity", "span": "is ascribed to some of the Mikados. It was not", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "Thus the Nakatomi family, who besides holding other high offices,", "span": "were the recognised vicars of the Mikado in the discharge", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "Ta-jikara no wo (hand-strength-male) is one of the few examples", "span": "of this class. He it was who, when the Sun-goddess", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Miya meant equally shrine and palace. Matsuri, a Shinto festival,", "span": "is the same word that we also find in Matsurigoto,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "Kannushi is the ordinary word for a Shinto priest. The", "span": "Kannushi are not celibates, and are not distinguishable from the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "In modern Japan, ancestor-worship is a comparatively rational cult, and", "span": "it is surely undesirable that missionaries should create for themselves", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "Other food-offerings were cakes, fruit, vegetables, edible seaweed, salt, water,", "span": "and the flesh of deer, pigs, hare, wild boar, and", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "The carriage (mikoshi) in which the deity, or rather his", "span": "shintai , is promenaded on the occasion of his annual", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "But there are abundant examples in the Yengishiki , and", "span": "other authorities, of the official liturgies known as norito ,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "Pilgrimages are an ancient institution in Japan. Even the Mikado", "span": "paid occasional visits to the shrines in or near Kioto.", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "His 65 \u2018etc.\u2019 puzzles me. I am unable to find", "span": "in the Ohoharahi the smallest trace of any of the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "Self-inflicted wounds, the cutting of dead bodies, or wounds inflicted", "span": "by others, caused uncleanness just as much as the wounding", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "Disease, especially leprosy (as in the Mosaic legislation), wounds and", "span": "sores involved various degrees of pollution. The death of a", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "He shut himself up in his house, refrained from speech", "span": "and noise and ate food cooked at a pure fire.", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.practice.7944ec", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "practice", "filler": "A modern Japanese writer says:\u2014 70 \u2018Anciently the Mikado received", "span": "the auspicious grain from the Gods of Heaven, and therewithal", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.planet.aa87bf", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "planet", "filler": "To some of these a black horse was offered as", "span": "a suggestion that black rain-clouds would be welcome. Ohoharahi ,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.element.307dd6", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "element", "filler": "Ho-shidzume no matsuri , or fire-calming-ceremony. The object of this", "span": "rite was to deprecate the destruction of the Imperial Palace", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.symbol.41756d", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "symbol", "filler": "In many private dwellings there is a Kami-dana (god-shelf) where", "span": "a harahi, consisting of a piece of wood from the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.concept.88f8c2", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "concept", "filler": "A tortoise-shell was afterwards substituted for the deer\u2019s shoulder-blade, in", "span": "imitation of China. There was attached to the palace a", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.text.d2a658", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "text", "filler": "They were sometimes used for political purposes. There is evidence", "span": "that the inspired person, generally a woman, delivered the divine", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.shinto_onmyodo.letter.048d50", "family_id": "shinto_onmyodo", "role": "letter", "filler": "Its principal founder was the famous K\u014db\u014d Daishi. At a", "span": "later time other similar schools or sects were originated which", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
