{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.concept.be6e1f", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "concept", "filler": "Thus we see that the primary religion, which is popularly", "span": "known as Paganism, was founded in the worship of personified", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.text.d942bb", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "text", "filler": "THE GEOCENTRIC SYSTEM OF NATURE. In constructing their system of", "span": "nature, the ancient Astronomers constituted it of the Earth, the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.letter.cf359b", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "letter", "filler": "vii. 11, and viii. 2, Job xxvi. 11, and Malachi", "span": "iii. 10. The Planets. Believing that the stars were but", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.practice.6e119a", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "practice", "filler": "An abbreviatory sign having been attached to each of these", "span": "constellations, the great celestial belt containing them was called \"the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.planet.68904c", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "planet", "filler": "THE SACRED NUMBERS 7 AND 12. In reference to the", "span": "planets, and the signs of the Zodiac, the numbers seven", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.element.2f513c", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "element", "filler": "In the Book of Revelation alone the number 7 is", "span": "repeated twenty-four times, and the number 12 fourteen times. THE", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.symbol.7c8b84", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Hence, designating that mythical being as the only begotten of", "span": "the Father, they personified him as God the Son, or", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.concept.be6e1f", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "concept", "filler": "Thus under various names, intended to represent God Sol in", "span": "relation to the diversified seasons, we find recorded in the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.text.d942bb", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "text", "filler": "\"Shall there be evil in a city, and the Lord", "span": "hath not done it?\" Amos iii., 6. Besides the title", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.letter.cf359b", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "letter", "filler": "Having ascribed to the imaginary incarnations of God Sol the", "span": "characteristics of heaven-descending, virgin-born, earth-walking, wonder-working, dying, resuscitated and ascending", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.practice.6e119a", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "practice", "filler": "When these fables were composed the Summer Solstice was in", "span": "the sign of Leo, and making the twelve labors begin", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.planet.68904c", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "planet", "filler": "Hence, comparing the first day of infantile life to the", "span": "shortest day of the year, it would naturally be expected", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
