{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.symbol.7c8b84", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "symbol", "filler": "In the observance of this festival the temples were adorned", "span": "with floral offerings; the Hilaries sang their joyful lays; the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.concept.be6e1f", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "concept", "filler": "Hence being observed but once a year, it was in", "span": "reality not an ordinance but an anniversary; and the fact", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.text.d942bb", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "text", "filler": "In the Christian calendar this personification is known as Thomas,", "span": "and a more specific dedication of the shortest day of", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.letter.cf359b", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "letter", "filler": "Such was the personification referred to in the Christian Gospel-story", "span": "as having been raised from the grave by the mandate,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.practice.6e119a", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "practice", "filler": "At this rate of precession, which modern, calculation has confirmed,", "span": "it requires 71 2-3 years for the Cardinal points to", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.planet.68904c", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "planet", "filler": "The Ram. By deducting 2,150 years from 6,450, we determine", "span": "that about 4,300 years; ago the Vernal Equinox entered the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.element.2f513c", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "element", "filler": "At each of the cardinal points there was a small", "span": "cross, and the lamb held in its uplifted fore-foot a", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.symbol.7c8b84", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Besides these, we have the checkered flooring or mosaic work,", "span": "representing the earth and its variegated face, which was introduced", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.concept.be6e1f", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "concept", "filler": "There are some who have gained themselves great reputation for", "span": "physic by their birth, as the \"seventh son of a", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.text.d942bb", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "text", "filler": "He had written a play, but airily, and without the", "span": "twenty years of arduous and persistent study declared by the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.letter.cf359b", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "letter", "filler": "And he was, moreover, presently quite fearless in the presence", "span": "of Saturn , quite unabashed beneath the glittering eye of", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.practice.6e119a", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "practice", "filler": "We find him now, on this fifteenth day of the", "span": "first month, aware of his revered grandmother\u2019s intrepid expedition to", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.planet.68904c", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "planet", "filler": "If you hadn\u2019t said that because of a certain conjunction", "span": "of planets\u2014or whatever it was\u2014in my horoscope, I should have", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.element.2f513c", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "element", "filler": "Malkiel\u2019s name on the envelope, have thrown the note down", "span": "a grating, and bolted before he reached the place, though", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.symbol.7c8b84", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "symbol", "filler": "\u201cThem that knows other let them declare it,\u201d she ejaculated.", "span": "\u201cI say again, as I did afore\u2014the homes that have", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.concept.be6e1f", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "concept", "filler": "Then all was not over yet. There was something still", "span": "in store for him. He sat up, pushed the creaming", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.text.d942bb", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "text", "filler": "Merillia\u2019s accident. In any case he answered firmly,\u2014 \u201cMalkiel the", "span": "Second, in Berkeley Square I had a relation\u2014an honoured grandmother.\u201d", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.letter.cf359b", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "letter", "filler": "Not at all,\u201d rejoined Malkiel, with icy formality. \u201cPray let", "span": "the fault be mine.\u201d \u201cI will not indeed. But let", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.practice.6e119a", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "practice", "filler": "\u201cWell, Malkiel the Second,\u201d continued the Prophet, recovering his composure", "span": "as he approached his coup , \u201cmy grandmother did have", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.planet.68904c", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "planet", "filler": "The Prophet grew really perturbed. He remembered his promise to", "span": "his grandmother and Sir Tiglath, and felt that he must", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.element.2f513c", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "element", "filler": "In consequence of Scorpio being in the sign of Sagittarius.", "span": "The crab will be very busy up till the third", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.symbol.7c8b84", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "symbol", "filler": "\u201cYou will trace the cycloidal curve of the planets\u2014can you", "span": "do that?\u201d The Prophet nodded. \u201cAs it affects her birthday,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.concept.be6e1f", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "concept", "filler": "He thinks her such a thoroughly sensible girl.\u201d \u201cBob! Does", "span": "he?\u201d said the Prophet, concealing a slight smile. \u201cYes. If", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.text.d942bb", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "text", "filler": "Ferdinand\u2019s special sanctum was prompted by the fact that, just", "span": "as he was speaking, he happened to see a bradawl", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.letter.cf359b", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "letter", "filler": "I don\u2019t know how many Christian Science Temples she hasn\u2019t", "span": "erected, or subscribed liberally to. She turns every table in", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.practice.6e119a", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "practice", "filler": "\u201cI am, Mr. Ferdinand,\u201d he replied, in a pale and", "span": "exhausted manner. \u201cThen tell me, Gustavus, have you ever lived", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.planet.68904c", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "planet", "filler": "Nature, with all her shining mysteries, her distant reticences and", "span": "revelations, calmed the turmoil within him. He looked upon the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.element.2f513c", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "element", "filler": "Leaning upon the sill of the window he found the", "span": "crab and\u2014breathing a short prayer for forgiveness\u2014committed his dear relation", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.symbol.7c8b84", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "symbol", "filler": "H\u2019m! We didn\u2019t arrive at any of this by our", "span": "observations, did we, Sophronia?\u201d \u201cDecidedly not,\u201d snapped Madame, haughtily. \u201cAnd", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.concept.be6e1f", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "concept", "filler": "\u201cI said this was a trap. I said it was", "span": "a rat-trap from the first.\u201d \u201cI knew he must be", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.astrology_west.text.d942bb", "family_id": "astrology_west", "role": "text", "filler": "My love,\u201d said Mr. Sagittarius, in a cracking voice, \u201cwe", "span": "are in it to-night, we are indeed; we are fairly", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.planet.9963c1", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "planet", "filler": "TO 330 A.D. BY F. LEGGE, F.S.A. (Honorary) Foreign Secretary", "span": "Society of Biblical Archaeology, Member of Council Royal Asiatic Society,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.element.b8c144", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "element", "filler": "\u2014Story of two first parts\u2014Pre-terrestrial acts of Jesus\u2014Incarnation and Second", "span": "Ascension with address of the Powers\u2014Arrangement of Heavenly Worlds and", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.symbol.0d86a0", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Without taking this accusation as literally correct, it is plain", "span": "that the chance of irresponsible power over those whom they", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.concept.8d904e", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "concept", "filler": "Marcion, the founder of the Marcionite Church, was a native", "span": "of Pontus. Saturnilus or Saturninus\u2014the name is spelt differently by", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.text.e00e53", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "text", "filler": "[38] , seemed likely to deliver us. The work thus", "span": "recovered bore the title of the Refutation of all Heresies", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.letter.343cfc", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "letter", "filler": "Their conclusions, although they do not seem to put the", "span": "matter entirely beyond doubt, have been accepted by many theological", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.practice.16c6d6", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "practice", "filler": "Later, when it came to the turn of the Christians", "span": "to dictate imperial edicts, the possession of heretical writings was", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.planet.9963c1", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "planet", "filler": "Although these several documents were evidently not all written at", "span": "one time and place, and cannot be assigned to a", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.element.b8c144", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "element", "filler": "But with these, there was now combined for the first", "span": "time the recognition of the divinity of One who, while", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.symbol.0d86a0", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "symbol", "filler": "How, then, were they to account for the fact that", "span": "their God Jesus, whether they considered Him as the Logos", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.concept.8d904e", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "concept", "filler": "Valentinus, from whose teaching, as we shall see, the principal", "span": "system of the Pistis Sophia was probably derived, also adhered", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.text.e00e53", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "text", "filler": "By doing so, they laid themselves open to the accusation", "span": "hurled at them with great virulence by the Church, that", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.letter.343cfc", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "letter", "filler": "These and other points which the post-Christian Gnostic sects seem", "span": "to have had in common [67] can therefore be accounted", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.practice.16c6d6", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "practice", "filler": "But the Fathers seldom thought of distinguishing between the opinions", "span": "of an heresiarch and those of his successors, and the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.planet.9963c1", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "planet", "filler": "It is also probable that between the time when the", "span": "Canonical Apocalypse was written and that of Origen and Hippolytus", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.element.b8c144", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "element", "filler": "It would not have been difficult for them to have", "span": "acquired at the same time from the Persian masters of", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.symbol.0d86a0", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "symbol", "filler": "With this view they went back to what is probably", "span": "the earliest philosophical theory of the origin of the universe,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.concept.8d904e", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "concept", "filler": "In the earliest Phrygian religion there seems little doubt that", "span": "the supreme goddess was originally considered to be bisexual, and", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.text.e00e53", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "text", "filler": "The later Ophite account of the production of this intermediary", "span": "power or messenger which we find in Irenaeus is that", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.letter.343cfc", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "letter", "filler": "But the Ophites went behind this conception, and made the", "span": "first confusion of the Divine light with matter the result", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.practice.16c6d6", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "practice", "filler": "They therefore called it Sinistra and declared it to be", "span": "feminine only [162] . Both traditions agreed that this Sophia", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.planet.9963c1", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "planet", "filler": "This so enraged 49 him that he glared in his", "span": "wrath upon the underlying dregs of matter, and his thought", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.element.b8c144", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "element", "filler": "Hence it was the casting-down to this earth of Ophiomorphus", "span": "which gave it life and shape, 51 and thus stamped", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.symbol.0d86a0", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "symbol", "filler": "On their doing so, he cast them out of Paradise,", "span": "and threw them down to this world together with the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.concept.8d904e", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "concept", "filler": "Such an one, they said after his death would be", "span": "born again not with a fleshly but with a spiritual", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.text.e00e53", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "text", "filler": "They who participate in these heavenly mysteries, says the Naassene", "span": "author, receive greater destinies than the others [206] . It", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.letter.343cfc", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "letter", "filler": "Thus Hippolytus tells us that the Naassenes \u201cfrequent the so-called", "span": "mysteries of the Great Mother, thinking that through what is", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.practice.16c6d6", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "practice", "filler": "This power, having pity on her repentance, implored the First", "span": "Man to send Christos to her assistance. This prayer was", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.planet.9963c1", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "planet", "filler": "Jesus was crucified; but Christos did not forget Him and", "span": "sent a certain power to Him, who raised Him in", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.element.b8c144", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "element", "filler": "Probably the very credulous Bishop of Constantia was misled by", "span": "some picture or amulet depicting a serpent with his tail", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.symbol.0d86a0", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Now she weeps and now rejoices Now she weeps and", "span": "now is judged Now she is judged and now is", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.concept.8d904e", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "concept", "filler": "This pantheistic doctrine may have been current in Phrygia and", "span": "traces of it may perhaps be found in the Anatolian", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.text.e00e53", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "text", "filler": "Only by laying aside his earthly part as Jesus had", "span": "done and becoming entirely pneumatic, could man attain to the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.letter.343cfc", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "letter", "filler": "It seems to have been chiefly composed of circles, those", "span": "in the uppermost part\u2014which Celsus says were those \u201cabove the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.practice.16c6d6", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "practice", "filler": "Although they differ somewhat in the arrangement of the circles,", "span": "both are agreed that the blue and yellow circles signify", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.planet.9963c1", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "planet", "filler": "This is specially described by Celsus; and if it surprises", "span": "anyone to find it thus placed above the planetary heavens,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.element.b8c144", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "element", "filler": "The remaining sphere, containing within itself ten circles in Matter\u2019s", "span": "reconstruction and seven in Father Giraud\u2019s, is however fully described.", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.symbol.0d86a0", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Let grace be with me, O Father, yea let it", "span": "be with me [247] !\u201d In passing through the next", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.concept.8d904e", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "concept", "filler": "Let grace be with me, O Father, yea let it", "span": "be with me [251] !\u201d To Ailoaios: \u201cO Ailoaios, ruler", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.text.e00e53", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "text", "filler": "To judge from Origen\u2019s remark that \u201cthey say there is", "span": "a sympathy (\u03c3\u03c5\u03bc\u03c0\u03ac\u03b8\u03b5\u03b9\u03b1) between the Star Phaenon ( i.e. Saturn)", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.letter.343cfc", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "letter", "filler": "Father Giraud asserts on the faith of some of the", "span": "smaller heresiologists and Conciliar Acts that they spread over the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.practice.16c6d6", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "practice", "filler": "Those Ophites who wished to obtain 78 proselytes among Christian", "span": "catechumens no doubt felt the advisability of not insisting upon", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.planet.9963c1", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "planet", "filler": "The same document shows us how the Ophites, while adopting", "span": "all the ideas of their predecessors the Orphics as to", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.element.b8c144", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "element", "filler": "A Gospel of Thomas , which is also extant, contains", "span": "only the account of miracles performed by Jesus in His", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.symbol.0d86a0", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Epiphanius attributes to the same sect of \u201cGnostici\u201d the use", "span": "of a Gospel of Perfection which \u201cothers\u201d\u2014the context shows that", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.concept.8d904e", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "concept", "filler": "The same dialectic had already been made use of by", "span": "the Orphics, by Philo of Alexandria, and by Simon Magus;", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.text.e00e53", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "text", "filler": "before mentioned and will be more fully described in Chapter", "span": "X , can only be explained by reference to them.", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.letter.343cfc", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "letter", "filler": "If we may judge from the writings of this last,", "span": "the expressed object of this school was to instil a", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.practice.16c6d6", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "practice", "filler": "The case is different with Antioch, where one Saturninus or", "span": "Satornilus\u2014the name is spelt differently by Irenaeus and Hippolytus\u2014seems to", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.planet.9963c1", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "planet", "filler": "This is the account of Irenaeus, not materially varied by", "span": "any of the other early writers on heresy, with the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.element.b8c144", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "element", "filler": "As for the third Sonhood, it remained in the Seed", "span": "of the World, which thereafter gave birth to the Great", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.symbol.0d86a0", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Maspero has shown, sometimes consists of eight, sometimes of ten,", "span": "and sometimes of a still more discrepant number of individuals", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.concept.8d904e", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "concept", "filler": "Basilides, therefore, forms a very important link between Simon Magus", "span": "and the pre-Christian Gnostics\u2014with whom Basilides was connected, as we", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.text.e00e53", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "text", "filler": "It is significant also that the mystic and probably cryptogrammatic", "span": "name Caulacau which the Naassene writer uses for the Saviour", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.letter.343cfc", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "letter", "filler": "To fill the gap thus left, he returned to the", "span": "older conception of the Ophites, and postulated a Bythos or", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.practice.16c6d6", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "practice", "filler": "odd and even) numbers alternately until it arrived at the", "span": "perfect harmony of ten [338] . Yet those who study", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.planet.9963c1", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "planet", "filler": "Valentinus himself, however, probably did not give Bythos a spouse", "span": "and held that he remained apart from and uplifted above", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.element.b8c144", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "element", "filler": "Yet a statement that Tertullian lets drop, as if accidentally,", "span": "may teach us to beware of taking Valentinus\u2019 supposed opinions", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.symbol.0d86a0", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Clement of Alexandria shows similar comprehensiveness when he said that", "span": "in the Christian faith there are some mysteries more excellent", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.concept.8d904e", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "concept", "filler": "Yet although it was through this lieutenant of the Unknown", "span": "Father that all things were made, he also was too", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.text.e00e53", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "text", "filler": "102 Before coming to this, however, it will be well", "span": "to say something here about the ideas that seem to", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.letter.343cfc", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "letter", "filler": "But the names of the male aeons are all epithets", "span": "or attributes peculiar to their father Nous, who is thus", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.practice.16c6d6", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "practice", "filler": "All the accounts of Valentinus\u2019 teaching that have reached us", "span": "seem to agree that Sophia\u2019s lapse was caused, according to", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.planet.9963c1", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "planet", "filler": "Christos or Christ and the Holy Spirit, should be put", "span": "forth by Nous and Aletheia to give form and direction", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.element.b8c144", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "element", "filler": "Hence she turned herself to prayers and supplications to Christos,", "span": "the being who had given her form, and these prayers", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.symbol.0d86a0", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "symbol", "filler": "He and his realm come immediately below that of Sophia", "span": "Without, here somewhat unexpectedly called the Ogdoad, where Sophia dwells", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.concept.8d904e", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "concept", "filler": "The Demiurge, as in the Ophite system, was not, indeed,", "span": "bad, but foolish and blind, not knowing what he did,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.text.e00e53", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "text", "filler": "Yet this is not a question of conduct or free", "span": "will, but of predestination, and seems to mark the chief", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.letter.343cfc", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "letter", "filler": "The consequences of this division upon the future of mankind", "span": "generally also differed materially from that of the Ophitic scheme.", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.practice.16c6d6", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "practice", "filler": "It is very probable, as M. Am\u00e9lineau has shown with", "span": "great attention to detail, that every system, perhaps every universe,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.planet.9963c1", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "planet", "filler": "As for His Mission, it seems to have consisted in", "span": "revealing to man the constitution of the worlds above him,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.element.b8c144", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "element", "filler": "Irenaeus, however, says that Valentinus came to Rome during the", "span": "papacy of Hyginus, flourished (\u1f24\u03ba\u03bc\u03b1\u03c3\u03b5) under that of Pius, and", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.symbol.0d86a0", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "symbol", "filler": "They further said that 119 the Dodecad or group of", "span": "twelve aeons, of whom Sophia was the last, emanated not", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.concept.8d904e", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "concept", "filler": "Valentinus seems in like manner to have lived in Rome", "span": "as a Christian teacher, as we have seen, for at", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.text.e00e53", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "text", "filler": "The long series of aeons constituting his Pleroma or Fulness", "span": "of the Godhead seems at first sight to present the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.letter.343cfc", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "letter", "filler": "This view derives great support from the way in which", "span": "Clement of Alexandria, Valentinus\u2019 countryman and the one among the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.practice.16c6d6", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "practice", "filler": "So far as can now be seen, he, like all", "span": "Egyptians, never lost sight of allegory in dealing with matters", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.planet.9963c1", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "planet", "filler": "But he went far beyond them in applying the same", "span": "method of interpretation to all the acts of Jesus recorded", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.element.b8c144", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "element", "filler": "It seems indeed plain that Valentinus never intended to break", "span": "with the Catholic Church and that it is not likely", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.symbol.0d86a0", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Of such was doubtless \u201cmy fair sister Flora\u201d (\u1f00\u03b4\u03b5\u03bb\u03c6\u03ae \u03bc\u03bf\u03c5", "span": "\u03ba\u03b1\u03bb\u1f74 \u03a6\u03bb\u03ce\u03c1\u03b1), 131 to whom Valentinus\u2019 successor Ptolemy wrote a", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.concept.8d904e", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "concept", "filler": "The native Egyptians, too, had for millennia been given to", "span": "mystic speculation about the nature of God and the destiny", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.text.e00e53", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "text", "filler": "Such a class is not that out of which martyrs", "span": "are made, and is sure sooner or later to acquiesce", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.letter.343cfc", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "letter", "filler": "written in Coptic [460] . On palaeographic grounds it is", "span": "said to be not earlier than the VIth century A.D.", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.practice.16c6d6", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "practice", "filler": "is generally known by that name [464] . The story", "span": "presented in these two documents, although uncompleted, is, so far", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.planet.9963c1", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "planet", "filler": "Jesus then proceeds to describe His own Incarnation. When speaking,", "span": "still in the shape of the angel Gabriel, with Mary", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.element.b8c144", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "element", "filler": "And now that the time is fulfilled, clothe thyself in", "span": "it! Come unto us, for we all stand near to", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.symbol.0d86a0", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "symbol", "filler": "And there is also within it the glory of the", "span": "name which is on the right, and of all those", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.concept.8d904e", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "concept", "filler": "Come then unto us quickly in order that we may", "span": "clothe thee with them according to the command of the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.text.e00e53", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "text", "filler": "If the author ever intended to discuss them further, he", "span": "has certainly not done so in the Pistis Sophia properly", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.letter.343cfc", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "letter", "filler": "The lower part of the same universe is called the", "span": "Kerasmos or Confusion, because here the light, which in the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.practice.16c6d6", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "practice", "filler": "This is a part of the universe the existence of", "span": "which Jesus conceals from His disciples until He receives his", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.planet.9963c1", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "planet", "filler": "Only one of these is named and this is the", "span": "inferior or female member of the last syzygy. She is", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.element.b8c144", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "element", "filler": "Below the starry world comes the Sphere of Heimarmene or", "span": "Destiny, so called apparently because both the earthly and heavenly", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.symbol.0d86a0", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Before leaving the Twelve Aeons, Jesus takes away from its", "span": "rulers a third part of their power, and alters their", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.concept.8d904e", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "concept", "filler": "Out of envy and jealousy of Pistis Sophia, he sends", "span": "forth from himself a great power with a lion\u2019s face", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.text.e00e53", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "text", "filler": "The powers of light sent by Jesus, however, defeat all", "span": "her enemies, and the archangels Gabriel and Michael bear her", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.letter.343cfc", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "letter", "filler": "But before describing these, it may be as well to", "span": "draw attention to the manifest likeness between the theology and", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.practice.16c6d6", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "practice", "filler": "Among the powers inferior to her the names and places", "span": "are changed, but the general arrangement remains nearly the same", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.planet.9963c1", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "planet", "filler": "One may even find a vivid reminiscence of the Valentinian", "span": "nomenclature in the name of Pistis Sophia herself, which combines", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.element.b8c144", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "element", "filler": "But it is plain that both must have been made", "span": "by or rather through Jesus, because it is stated in", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.symbol.0d86a0", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "symbol", "filler": "A further parallel may be found in Hippolytus\u2019 other statement", "span": "from Valentinus that Jesus gave this \u201csupplication\u201d power over the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.concept.8d904e", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "concept", "filler": "What need then to elaborate the description of its most", "span": "malignant ministers? The joys of the elect in the world", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.text.e00e53", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "text", "filler": "The Greek word \u03bc\u03c5\u03c3\u03c4\u03ae\u03c1\u03b9\u03bf\u03bd, which is that used in the", "span": "Coptic MS. , does not seem to mean etymologically more", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.letter.343cfc", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "letter", "filler": "In any event, the rite was looked upon by Catholic", "span": "and heretic alike as an initiation or commencement of the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.practice.16c6d6", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "practice", "filler": "So the late Dr Hatch, writing of baptism in this", "span": "connection, says: \u201cThe expressions which the more literary ages have", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.planet.9963c1", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "planet", "filler": "He is a man in the Cosmos, but he is", "span": "not of the Cosmos, and verily I say unto you,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.element.b8c144", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "element", "filler": "These mysteries of the light are open to the whole", "span": "world and there is some reason for thinking they are", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.symbol.0d86a0", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Wherefore I said unto you aforetime: Renounce the whole world", "span": "and all the matter that is therein lest ye add", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.concept.8d904e", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "concept", "filler": "So was the peculiar theory that the lesser gods were", "span": "the limbs or members of the Supreme [597] . An", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.text.e00e53", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "text", "filler": "Even the doctrine in the Pistis Sophia that the dead", "span": "had to exhibit a \u201cseal\u201d as well as a \u201cdefence\u201d", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.letter.343cfc", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "letter", "filler": "Now the first direct and acknowledged quotation 178 from St", "span": "John\u2019s Gospel that we have is that made by Theophilus,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.practice.16c6d6", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "practice", "filler": "is called Pistis Sophia instead of Sophia only need not", "span": "hinder us from identifying this with the work presumably referred", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.planet.9963c1", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "planet", "filler": "The name of Ecclesia or the Church is given not", "span": "only to a particular aeon in the Pleroma, but also", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.element.b8c144", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "element", "filler": "Jesus \u201cstanding on the shore of the sea Ocean,\u201d then", "span": "makes invocation to the \u201cFather of every Fatherhood, boundless light,\u201d", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.symbol.0d86a0", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "symbol", "filler": "There is also given here a 184 very curious account", "span": "of man\u2019s invisible part, which is said to be made", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.concept.8d904e", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "concept", "filler": "diabolic, origin is here recommended as a means to be", "span": "employed under certain safeguards for the purpose of converting \u201cthe", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.text.e00e53", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "text", "filler": "Oddly enough, however, he gives an explanation of the myth", "span": "of the two springs of memory and oblivion that we", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.letter.343cfc", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "letter", "filler": "And the servants of the Sphere lead it into the", "span": "water which is below the Sphere, that the boiling steam", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.practice.16c6d6", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "practice", "filler": "It is also to be noted that the annotator has", "span": "written upon the blank leaf which separates the first and", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.planet.9963c1", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "planet", "filler": "The same remarks apply with but little modification to some", "span": "other fragments of Gnostic writings which have come down to", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.element.b8c144", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "element", "filler": "To enter into the controversy raised by this diversity of", "span": "opinion would take one outside the limits of the present", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.symbol.0d86a0", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Then he created the true habitation within it [651] ,", "span": "the Place of Repentance (Metanoia) within it, the Place of", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.concept.8d904e", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "concept", "filler": "Another large fragment in the Bruce Papyrus is also connected", "span": "with that which has been called above the Texts of", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.text.e00e53", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "text", "filler": "But the Texts of the Saviour , as we have", "span": "seen, also mention Pistis Sophia in such a way as", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.letter.343cfc", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "letter", "filler": "Both M. Am\u00e9lineau and Dr Schmidt are agreed that the", "span": "Coptic Papyrus is a translation from Greek originals; and M.", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.practice.16c6d6", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "practice", "filler": "Thus to quote again from what Dr Schmidt calls the", "span": "Second Book of Je\u00fb, Jesus imparts to His disciples the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.planet.9963c1", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "planet", "filler": "Those who were not so rich or so lucky were", "span": "thought to be parcelled out, like the fellahin of that", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.element.b8c144", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "element", "filler": "Say unto them that abandon the doctrines of truth of", "span": "the First Mystery \u2018Woe unto you, for your torment shall", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.symbol.0d86a0", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Hence there was not one God; but two Gods. One", "span": "of these was the Supreme Being, perfect in power as", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.concept.8d904e", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "concept", "filler": "But as this might seem like a defeat of the", "span": "Supreme Being by His inferior, he was forced to accept", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.text.e00e53", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "text", "filler": "Everywhere, it would seem, he took the Biblical texts that", "span": "he quotes at their literal meaning and never seems to", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.letter.343cfc", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "letter", "filler": "The case was different with Apelles, who was certainly later", "span": "in date than Marcion and perhaps succeeded him in the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.practice.16c6d6", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "practice", "filler": "The same tendency to compromise is evident in Apelles\u2019 willingness", "span": "to use the books of both the Old and the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.planet.9963c1", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "planet", "filler": "Those who trust in Him that was crucified will be", "span": "saved, if only they do good works [758] .\u201d Herein", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.element.b8c144", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "element", "filler": "That many of Marcion\u2019s ideas have been revived in our", "span": "own day is likely enough, and this opinion has been", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.symbol.0d86a0", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "symbol", "filler": "It is, however, impossible to speak with certainty on such", "span": "a point in the absence of any writings by persons", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.concept.8d904e", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "concept", "filler": "It is therefore extremely probable that the Mithraists figured Ahriman", "span": "as ruling the earth from the sphere immediately outside it,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.text.e00e53", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "text", "filler": "This idea appears plainly in the Papyrus quoted above, where", "span": "the Mithraist is represented as an eagle who flies upwards", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.letter.343cfc", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "letter", "filler": "If we may read into the tradition something which is", "span": "not expressed there, but which seems to follow logically from", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.practice.16c6d6", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "practice", "filler": "The Mahommedan source, here fuller than the Christian, tells us", "span": "that the Darkness remained in an unorganized condition for ages,", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.planet.9963c1", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "planet", "filler": "Both luminaries bear these elements into the Column of Praises", "span": "or Glory which is perpetually mounting from the Sun to", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.element.b8c144", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "element", "filler": "The stars are also in the Christian tradition fashioned out", "span": "of the purer part of the Light which was not", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.symbol.0d86a0", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "symbol", "filler": "There is evidently a reference here to some legend of", "span": "which we have lost the trace [1063] , and the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.concept.8d904e", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "concept", "filler": "Their prayer was heard, and Jesus was sent upon earth", "span": "\u201caccompanied by a god,\u201d with whose aid the Archons were", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.text.e00e53", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "text", "filler": "In the sequel, one of the Angels had relations with", "span": "the Wisdom of the World and begot two daughters, called", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.letter.343cfc", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "letter", "filler": "From this Prof. Kessler, who perhaps devoted more attention to", "span": "the Manichaean religion than any living scholar, built up the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.practice.16c6d6", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "practice", "filler": "And whoso receives it, distinguishes between good and evil. Yet", "span": "the Cosmos itself is not of God, but it was", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.planet.9963c1", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "planet", "filler": "But there is much plausibility in M. Cumont\u2019s theory that", "span": "this Third Legate or Sr\u00f4sh is supposed until that event", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.element.b8c144", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "element", "filler": "One regards the two great angels, here called Khrostag and", "span": "Padvaktag [1205] or the Appellant and Respondent, who are mentioned", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.symbol.0d86a0", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "symbol", "filler": "Then the germs already present in small fraternities like those", "span": "of the Orphics and the Essenes blossomed forth into the", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.concept.8d904e", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "concept", "filler": "1; called the Mother by Valentinus, ii. 112 n. 3;", "span": "the Sophia Without of Valentinus, ii. 117 n. 2; baptism", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.text.e00e53", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "text", "filler": "325 ; slayer of monster, ii. 329 Adonai, epithet of", "span": "Zeus in Mag. Pap., i. 106; in Coptic, ii. 46", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.letter.343cfc", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "letter", "filler": "195 . See Zodiac Aerodios, power mentioned in Bruce Papyrus,", "span": "ii. 191 Aeschines, son of Glaucothea, i. 22; Demosthenes\u2019 invective", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.practice.16c6d6", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "practice", "filler": "278 ; likeness of representation of, to Manichaean Satan, ii.", "span": "291 . See Goshurun Ahura Mazda, the Omniscient Lord, i.", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
{"pair_id": "corr.coptic_gnostic.planet.9963c1", "family_id": "coptic_gnostic", "role": "planet", "filler": "18; religious associations follow conquests of, i. 22-26 sqq. ;", "span": "his work in Egypt, i. 29, 44; his probable plans", "atom_id": null, "epistemic": "OBSERVED"}
